\s1 Nehemiah’s Prayer
\r \ref Deuteronomy 30:1–10|DEU 30:1-10\ref*)
\p \v 1 \rb These are the words|דִּבְרֵ֥י\rb* \rb of Nehemiah|נְחֶמְיָ֖ה\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Hacaliah:|חֲכַלְיָ֑ה\rb*
\p \rb |וַיְהִ֤י\rb* \rb In the month|בְחֹֽדֶשׁ־\rb* \rb of Chislev,|כִּסְלֵו\rb*\f + \fr 1:1 \fqa Chislev \ft is the ninth month of the Hebrew lunar calendar, usually occurring within the months of November and December.\f* \rb in the twentieth|עֶשְׂרִ֔ים\rb* \rb year,|שְׁנַ֣ת\rb* \rb while I|וַאֲנִ֥י\rb* \rb was|הָיִ֖יתִי\rb* \rb in the citadel|הַבִּירָֽה׃\rb* \rb of Susa,|בְּשׁוּשַׁ֥ן\rb* \v 2 \rb Hanani,|חֲנָ֜נִי\rb* \rb one|אֶחָ֧ד\rb* \rb of my brothers,|מֵאַחַ֛י\rb*\rb |ה֥וּא\rb* \rb arrived|וַיָּבֹ֨א\rb* \rb with men|וַאֲנָשִׁ֖ים\rb* \rb from Judah.|מִֽיהוּדָ֑ה\rb* \rb So I questioned them|וָאֶשְׁאָלֵ֞ם\rb* \rb about|עַל־\rb* \rb the remnant|הַפְּלֵיטָ֛ה\rb* \rb of the Jews|הַיְּהוּדִ֧ים\rb* \rb who|אֲשֶֽׁר־\rb* \rb had survived|נִשְׁאֲר֥וּ\rb* \rb the exile,|הַשֶּׁ֖בִי\rb* \rb and also about|וְעַל־\rb* \rb Jerusalem.|יְרוּשָׁלִָֽם׃\rb*
\p \v 3 \rb And they told|וַיֹּאמְרוּ֮\rb* \rb me,|לִי֒\rb* \rb “The remnant|הַֽנִּשְׁאָרִ֞ים\rb* \rb who|אֲשֶֽׁר־\rb* \rb survived|נִשְׁאֲר֤וּ\rb*\rb |מִן־\rb* \rb the exile|הַשְּׁבִי֙\rb* \rb are there|שָׁ֣ם\rb* \rb in the province,|בַּמְּדִינָ֔ה\rb* \rb in great|גְדֹלָ֖ה\rb* \rb trouble|בְּרָעָ֥ה\rb* \rb and disgrace.|וּבְחֶרְפָּ֑ה\rb* \rb The wall|וְחוֹמַ֤ת\rb* \rb of Jerusalem|יְרוּשָׁלִַ֙ם֙\rb* \rb is broken down,|מְפֹרָ֔צֶת\rb* \rb and its gates|וּשְׁעָרֶ֖יהָ\rb* \rb have been burned|נִצְּת֥וּ\rb* \rb with fire.”|בָאֵֽשׁ׃\rb*
\p \v 4 \rb |וַיְהִ֞י\rb* \rb When I heard|כְּשָׁמְעִ֣י׀\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb these|הָאֵ֗לֶּה\rb* \rb words,|הַדְּבָרִ֣ים\rb* \rb I sat down|יָשַׁ֙בְתִּי֙\rb* \rb and wept.|וָֽאֶבְכֶּ֔ה\rb* \rb I mourned|וָאֶתְאַבְּלָ֖ה\rb* \rb for days,|יָמִ֑ים\rb*\rb |וָֽאֱהִ֥י\rb* \rb fasting|צָם֙\rb* \rb and praying|וּמִתְפַּלֵּ֔ל\rb* \rb before|לִפְנֵ֖י\rb* \rb the God|אֱלֹהֵ֥י\rb* \rb of heaven.|הַשָּׁמָֽיִם׃\rb*
\p \v 5 \rb Then I said:|וָאֹמַ֗ר\rb*
\pmo \rb “O|אָֽנָּ֤א\rb* \rb LORD,|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb God|אֱלֹהֵ֣י\rb* \rb of heaven,|הַשָּׁמַ֔יִם\rb* \rb the great|הַגָּד֖וֹל\rb* \rb and awesome|וְהַנּוֹרָ֑א\rb* \rb God|הָאֵ֥ל\rb* \rb who keeps|שֹׁמֵ֤ר\rb* \rb His covenant|הַבְּרִית֙\rb* \rb of loving devotion|וָחֶ֔סֶד\rb*\f + \fr 1:5 \ft Forms of the Hebrew \fqa chesed \ft are translated here and in most cases throughout the Scriptures as \fqa loving devotion\ft ; the range of meaning includes \fqa love\ft , \fqa goodness\ft , \fqa kindness\ft , \fqa faithfulness\ft , and \fqa mercy\ft , as well as \fqa loyalty to a covenant\ft .\f* \rb with those who love Him|לְאֹהֲבָ֖יו\rb* \rb and keep|וּלְשֹׁמְרֵ֥י\rb* \rb His commandments,|מִצְוֺתָֽיו׃\rb* \v 6 \rb let Your eyes|וְֽעֵינֶ֪יךָ\rb* \rb be|תְּהִ֣י\rb*\rb |נָ֣א\rb* \rb open|פְתֻוּח֟וֹת\rb* \rb and Your ears|אָזְנְךָֽ־\rb* \rb attentive|קַשֶּׁ֣בֶת\rb* \rb to hear|לִשְׁמֹ֣עַ\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb the prayer|תְּפִלַּ֣ת\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb I,|אָנֹכִי֩\rb* \rb Your servant,|עַבְדְּךָ֡\rb* \rb now|הַיּוֹם֙\rb* \rb pray|מִתְפַּלֵּ֨ל\rb* \rb before You|לְפָנֶ֤יךָ\rb* \rb day|יוֹמָ֣ם\rb* \rb and night|וָלַ֔יְלָה\rb* \rb for|עַל־\rb* \rb Your servants,|עֲבָדֶ֑יךָ\rb* \rb the Israelites.|בְּנֵ֥י\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל\rb*
