\p \rb (At that time I|וַאֲנִ֛י\rb* \rb was|הָיִ֥יתִי\rb* \rb the cupbearer|מַשְׁקֶ֖ה\rb* \rb to the king.)|לַמֶּֽלֶךְ׃פ\rb*
\c 2
\s1 Nehemiah Sent to Jerusalem
\p \v 1 \rb Now|וַיְהִ֣י׀\rb* \rb in the month|בְּחֹ֣דֶשׁ\rb* \rb of Nisan,|נִיסָ֗ן\rb*\f + \fr 2:1 \fqa Nisan \ft is the first month of the Hebrew lunar calendar, usually occurring within the months of March and April.\f* \rb in the twentieth|עֶשְׂרִ֛ים\rb* \rb year|שְׁנַ֥ת\rb* \rb of King|הַמֶּ֖לֶךְ\rb* \rb Artaxerxes,|לְאַרְתַּחְשַׁ֥סְתְּא\rb* \rb when wine|יַ֣יִן\rb* \rb was set before him,|לְפָנָ֑יו\rb* \rb I took|וָאֶשָּׂ֤א\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the wine|הַיַּ֙יִן֙\rb* \rb and gave|וָאֶתְּנָ֣ה\rb* \rb it to the king.|לַמֶּ֔לֶךְ\rb* \rb I had never|וְלֹא־\rb* \rb been|הָיִ֥יתִי\rb* \rb sad|רַ֖ע\rb* \rb in his presence,|לְפָנָֽיו׃\rb* \v 2 \rb so the king|הַמֶּ֜לֶךְ\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּאמֶר֩\rb* \rb to me,|לִ֨י\rb* \rb “Why is|מַדּ֣וּעַ׀\rb* \rb your face|פָּנֶ֣יךָ\rb* \rb sad,|רָעִ֗ים\rb* \rb though you are|וְאַתָּה֙\rb* \rb not|אֵֽינְךָ֣\rb* \rb ill?|חוֹלֶ֔ה\rb* \rb This|זֶ֔ה\rb* \rb could only be|אֵ֣ין\rb*\rb |כִּי־\rb*\rb |אִ֖ם\rb* \rb sadness|רֹ֣עַֽ\rb* \rb of the heart.”|לֵ֑ב\rb*
\p \rb I was overwhelmed with fear|וָאִירָ֖א\rb*\rb |הַרְבֵּ֥ה\rb*\rb |מְאֹֽד׃\rb* \v 3 \rb and replied|וָאֹמַ֣ר\rb* \rb to the king,|לַמֶּ֔לֶךְ\rb* \rb “May the king|הַמֶּ֖לֶךְ\rb* \rb live forever!|יִחְיֶ֑ה\rb*\rb |לְעוֹלָ֣ם\rb* \rb Why|מַדּ֜וּעַ\rb* \rb should I not|לֹא־\rb* \rb be sad|יֵרְע֣וּ\rb*\rb |פָנַ֗י\rb* \rb when|אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb the city|הָעִ֜יר\rb* \rb where|בֵּית־\rb* \rb my fathers|אֲבֹתַי֙\rb* \rb are buried|קִבְר֤וֹת\rb* \rb lies in ruins,|חֲרֵבָ֔ה\rb* \rb and its gates|וּשְׁעָרֶ֖יהָ\rb* \rb have been destroyed|אֻכְּל֥וּ\rb* \rb by fire?”|בָאֵֽשׁ׃ס\rb*
\p \v 4 \rb “What|מַה־\rb*\rb |זֶּ֖ה\rb* \rb is your|אַתָּ֣ה\rb* \rb request?”|מְבַקֵּ֑שׁ\rb* \rb replied|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb*\rb |לִי֙\rb* \rb the king.|הַמֶּ֔לֶךְ\rb*\rb |עַל־\rb*
\p \rb So I prayed|וָֽאֶתְפַּלֵּ֔ל\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the God|אֱלֹהֵ֖י\rb* \rb of heaven|הַשָּׁמָֽיִם׃\rb* \v 5 \rb and answered|וָאֹמַ֣ר\rb* \rb the king,|לַמֶּ֔לֶךְ\rb* \rb “If|אִם־\rb* \rb it pleases|ט֔וֹב\rb* \rb the king,|הַמֶּ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb and if|וְאִם־\rb* \rb your servant|עַבְדְּךָ֖\rb* \rb has found favor|יִיטַ֥ב\rb* \rb in your sight,|לְפָנֶ֑יךָ\rb* \rb I ask that|אֲשֶׁ֧ר\rb* \rb you send me|תִּשְׁלָחֵ֣נִי\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Judah,|יְהוּדָ֗ה\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the city|עִ֛יר\rb* \rb where my fathers|אֲבֹתַ֖י\rb* \rb are buried,|קִבְר֥וֹת\rb* \rb so that I may rebuild it.”|וְאֶבְנֶֽנָּה׃\rb*
\p \v 6 \rb Then the king,|הַמֶּ֜לֶךְ\rb* \rb with the queen|וְהַשֵּׁגַ֣ל׀\rb* \rb seated|יוֹשֶׁ֣בֶת\rb* \rb beside him,|אֶצְל֗וֹ\rb* \rb asked|וַיֹּאמֶר֩\rb* \rb me,|לִ֨י\rb* \rb “How long|עַד־\rb*\rb |מָתַ֛י\rb* \rb will your journey|מַֽהֲלָכֲךָ֖\rb* \rb take,|יִהְיֶ֥ה\rb* \rb and when|וּמָתַ֣י\rb* \rb will you return?”|תָּשׁ֑וּב\rb* \rb So it pleased|וַיִּיטַ֤ב\rb*\rb |לִפְנֵֽי־\rb* \rb the king|הַמֶּ֙לֶךְ֙\rb* \rb to send me,|וַיִּשְׁלָחֵ֔נִי\rb* \rb and I set|וָֽאֶתְּנָ֥ה\rb* \rb a time.|זְמָֽן׃\rb*
\p \v 7 \rb I also said|וָאוֹמַר֮\rb* \rb to him,|לַמֶּלֶךְ֒\rb* \rb “If|אִם־\rb* \rb it pleases|ט֔וֹב\rb* \rb the king,|הַמֶּ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb may letters|אִגְּרוֹת֙\rb* \rb be given|יִתְּנוּ־\rb* \rb to me|לִ֔י\rb* \rb for|עַֽל־\rb* \rb the governors|פַּחֲו֖וֹת\rb* \rb west|עֵ֣בֶר\rb* \rb of the Euphrates,|הַנָּהָ֑ר\rb*\f + \fr 2:7 \ft Hebrew \fqa beyond the River\ft ; also in verse 9\f* \rb so that|אֲשֶׁר֙\rb* \rb they will grant me safe passage|יַעֲבִיר֔וּנִי\rb* \rb until|עַ֥ד\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb I reach|אָב֖וֹא\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb Judah.|יְהוּדָֽה׃\rb* \v 8 \rb And may I have a letter|וְאִגֶּ֡רֶת\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Asaph,|אָסָף֩\rb* \rb keeper|שֹׁמֵ֨ר\rb* \rb of the king’s|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb*\rb |לַמֶּ֗לֶךְ\rb* \rb forest,|הַפַּרְדֵּ֜ס\rb* \rb so that|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb he will give|יִתֶּן־\rb* \rb me|לִ֣י\rb* \rb timber|עֵצִ֡ים\rb* \rb to make beams|לְ֠קָרוֹת\rb* \rb for|אֶת־\rb* \rb the gates|שַׁעֲרֵ֨י\rb* \rb of the citadel|הַבִּירָ֤ה\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb to the temple,|לַבַּ֙יִת֙\rb* \rb for the city|הָעִ֔יר\rb* \rb wall,|וּלְחוֹמַ֣ת\rb* \rb and for the house|וְלַבַּ֖יִת\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb I will occupy.”|אָב֣וֹא\rb*\rb |אֵלָ֑יו\rb*
\p \rb And because the gracious|הַטּוֹבָ֥ה\rb* \rb hand|כְּיַד־\rb* \rb of my God|אֱלֹהַ֖י\rb* \rb was upon me,|עָלָֽי׃\rb* \rb the king|הַמֶּ֔לֶךְ\rb* \rb granted|וַיִּתֶּן־\rb* \rb my requests.|לִ֣י\rb*
\p \v 9 \rb Then I went|וָֽאָב֗וֹא\rb* \rb to|אֶֽל־\rb* \rb the governors|פַּֽחֲווֹת֙\rb* \rb west|עֵ֣בֶר\rb* \rb of the Euphrates|הַנָּהָ֔ר\rb* \rb and gave|וָאֶתְּנָ֣ה\rb* \rb them|לָהֶ֔ם\rb*\rb |אֵ֖ת\rb* \rb the king’s|הַמֶּ֑לֶךְ\rb* \rb letters.|אִגְּר֣וֹת\rb* \rb The king|הַמֶּ֔לֶךְ\rb* \rb had also sent|וַיִּשְׁלַ֤ח\rb* \rb army|חַ֖יִל\rb* \rb officers|שָׂ֥רֵי\rb* \rb and cavalry|וּפָרָשִֽׁים׃פ\rb* \rb with me.|עִמִּי֙\rb*
\p \v 10 \rb But when Sanballat|סַנְבַלַּ֣ט\rb* \rb the Horonite|הַחֹרֹנִ֗י\rb* \rb and Tobiah|וְטֽוֹבִיָּה֙\rb* \rb the Ammonite|הָֽעַמֹּנִ֔י\rb* \rb official|הָעֶ֣בֶד\rb* \rb heard about this,|וַיִּשְׁמַ֞ע\rb* \rb they were deeply|גְדֹלָ֑ה\rb* \rb disturbed|וַיֵּ֥רַע\rb*\rb |לָהֶ֖ם\rb*\rb |רָעָ֣ה\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb someone|אָדָ֔ם\rb* \rb had come|בָּ֥א\rb* \rb to seek|לְבַקֵּ֥שׁ\rb* \rb the well-being|טוֹבָ֖ה\rb*\rb |לִבְנֵ֥י\rb* \rb of the Israelites.|יִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃\rb*
\s1 Nehemiah Inspects the Walls
\p \v 11 \rb After I had arrived|וָאָב֖וֹא\rb* \rb in|אֶל־\rb* \rb Jerusalem|יְרוּשָׁלִָ֑ם\rb* \rb and had been|וָאֱהִי־\rb* \rb there|שָׁ֖ם\rb* \rb three|שְׁלֹשָֽׁה׃\rb* \rb days,|יָמִ֥ים\rb* \v 12 \rb I|אֲנִי֮\rb* \rb set out|וָאָק֣וּם׀\rb* \rb at night|לַ֗יְלָה\rb* \rb with|עִמִּי֒\rb* \rb a few|מְעַט֮\rb* \rb men.|וַאֲנָשִׁ֣ים׀\rb* \rb I did not|וְלֹא־\rb* \rb tell|הִגַּ֣דְתִּי\rb* \rb anyone|לְאָדָ֔ם\rb* \rb what|מָ֗ה\rb* \rb my God|אֱלֹהַי֙\rb* \rb had laid|נֹתֵ֣ן\rb* \rb on|אֶל־\rb* \rb my heart|לִבִּ֔י\rb* \rb to do|לַעֲשׂ֖וֹת\rb* \rb for Jerusalem.|לִירוּשָׁלִָ֑ם\rb* \rb The only|כִּ֚י\rb*\rb |אִם־\rb* \rb animal|וּבְהֵמָה֙\rb*\rb |אֵ֣ין\rb* \rb with me|עִמִּ֔י\rb* \rb was the one|הַבְּהֵמָ֔ה\rb* \rb on which|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb I|אֲנִ֖י\rb* \rb was riding.|רֹכֵ֥ב\rb*
\p \v 13 \rb So I went out|וָאֵצְאָ֨ה\rb* \rb at night|לַ֗יְלָה\rb* \rb through the Valley|הַגַּ֜יא\rb* \rb Gate|בְשַֽׁעַר־\rb* \rb toward|וְאֶל־\rb*\rb |פְּנֵי֙\rb* \rb the Well|עֵ֣ין\rb* \rb of the Serpent|הַתַּנִּ֔ין\rb*\f + \fr 2:13 \ft Or \fqa Dragon \ft or \fqa Jackal\f*\rb |וְאֶל־\rb* \rb and the Dung|הָאַשְׁפֹּ֑ת\rb*\rb |וָאֱהִ֨י\rb* \rb Gate,|שַׁ֖עַר\rb* \rb and I inspected|שֹׂבֵ֜ר\rb* \rb the walls|בְּחוֹמֹ֤ת\rb* \rb of Jerusalem|יְרוּשָׁלִַ֙ם֙\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb had been broken down|הַמְפֹרוָצִים\rb* \rb and the gates|וּשְׁעָרֶ֖יהָ\rb* \rb that had been destroyed|אֻכְּל֥וּ\rb* \rb by fire.|בָאֵֽשׁ׃\rb*
\p \v 14 \rb Then I went on|וָאֶֽעֱבֹר֙\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the Fountain|הָעַ֔יִן\rb*\rb |וְאֶל־\rb* \rb Gate|שַׁ֣עַר\rb* \rb and the King’s|הַמֶּ֑לֶךְ\rb* \rb Pool,|בְּרֵכַ֖ת\rb* \rb but there was no|וְאֵין־\rb* \rb room|מָק֥וֹם\rb* \rb for the animal|לַבְּהֵמָ֖ה\rb* \rb under me|תַּחְתָּֽי׃\rb* \rb to get through;|לַעֲבֹ֥ר\rb* \v 15 \rb so I|וָאֱהִ֨י\rb* \rb went up|עֹלֶ֤ה\rb* \rb the valley|בַנַּ֙חַל֙\rb* \rb by night|לַ֔יְלָה\rb* \rb and|וָאֱהִ֥י\rb* \rb inspected|שֹׂבֵ֖ר\rb* \rb the wall.|בַּחוֹמָ֑ה\rb* \rb Then I headed back|וָאָשׁ֗וּב\rb* \rb and reentered|וָאָב֛וֹא\rb*\rb |וָאָשֽׁוּב׃\rb* \rb through the Valley|הַגַּ֖יְא\rb* \rb Gate.|בְּשַׁ֥עַר\rb*
\p \v 16 \rb The officials|וְהַסְּגָנִ֗ים\rb* \rb did not|לֹ֤א\rb* \rb know|יָדְעוּ֙\rb* \rb where|אָ֣נָה\rb* \rb I had gone|הָלַ֔כְתִּי\rb* \rb or what|וּמָ֖ה\rb* \rb I|אֲנִ֣י\rb* \rb was doing,|עֹשֶׂ֑ה\rb* \rb for I had not|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb yet|עַד־\rb*\rb |כֵּ֖ן\rb* \rb told|הִגַּֽדְתִּי׃\rb* \rb the Jews|וְלַיְּהוּדִ֨ים\rb* \rb or priests|וְלַכֹּהֲנִ֜ים\rb* \rb or nobles|וְלַחֹרִ֣ים\rb* \rb or officials|וְלַסְּגָנִ֗ים\rb* \rb or any other|וּלְיֶ֙תֶר֙\rb*\rb |עֹשֵׂ֣ה\rb* \rb workers.|הַמְּלָאכָ֔ה\rb* \v 17 \rb Then I said|וָאוֹמַ֣ר\rb* \rb to them,|אֲלֵהֶ֗ם\rb* \rb “You|אַתֶּ֤ם\rb* \rb see|רֹאִים֙\rb* \rb the trouble|הָרָעָה֙\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb we are|אֲנַ֣חְנוּ\rb* \rb in.|בָ֔הּ\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֤ר\rb* \rb Jerusalem|יְרוּשָׁלִַ֙ם֙\rb* \rb lies in ruins,|חֲרֵבָ֔ה\rb* \rb and its gates|וּשְׁעָרֶ֖יהָ\rb* \rb have been burned down.|נִצְּת֣וּ\rb*\rb |בָאֵ֑שׁ\rb* \rb Come,|לְכ֗וּ\rb* \rb let us rebuild|וְנִבְנֶה֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the wall|חוֹמַ֣ת\rb* \rb of Jerusalem,|יְרוּשָׁלִַ֔ם\rb* \rb so that we will no|וְלֹא־\rb* \rb longer|ע֖וֹד\rb* \rb be|נִהְיֶ֥ה\rb* \rb a disgrace.”|חֶרְפָּֽה׃\rb*
\p \v 18 \rb I also told|וָאַגִּ֨יד\rb* \rb them|לָהֶ֜ם\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb about|אֲשֶׁר־\rb*\rb |הִיא֙\rb* \rb the gracious|טוֹבָ֣ה\rb* \rb hand|יַ֣ד\rb* \rb of my God|אֱלֹהַ֗י\rb* \rb upon me,|עָלַ֔י\rb* \rb and|וְאַף־\rb*\rb |דִּבְרֵ֥י\rb* \rb what|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb the king|הַמֶּ֖לֶךְ\rb* \rb had said|אָֽמַר־\rb* \rb to me.|לִ֑י\rb*
\p \rb “Let us start|נָק֣וּם\rb* \rb rebuilding,”|וּבָנִ֔ינוּ\rb* \rb they replied,|וַיֹּֽאמְרוּ֙\rb* \rb and they set|וַיְחַזְּק֥וּ\rb* \rb their hands|יְדֵיהֶ֖ם\rb* \rb to this good work.|לַטּוֹבָֽה׃פ\rb*
\p \v 19 \rb But when Sanballat|סַנְבַלַּ֨ט\rb* \rb the Horonite,|הַחֹרֹנִ֜י\rb* \rb Tobiah|וְטֹבִיָּ֣ה׀\rb* \rb the Ammonite|הָֽעַמּוֹנִ֗י\rb* \rb official,|הָעֶ֣בֶד\rb* \rb and Geshem|וְגֶ֙שֶׁם֙\rb* \rb the Arab|הָֽעַרְבִ֔י\rb* \rb heard about this,|וַיִּשְׁמַע֩\rb* \rb they mocked|וַיַּלְעִ֣גוּ\rb* \rb us|לָ֔נוּ\rb* \rb and ridiculed|וַיִּבְז֖וּ\rb* \rb us,|עָלֵ֑ינוּ\rb* \rb saying,|וַיֹּאמְר֗וּ\rb* \rb “What|מָֽה־\rb*\rb |הַדָּבָ֤ר\rb* \rb is this|הַזֶּה֙\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb you are|אַתֶּ֣ם\rb* \rb doing?|עֹשִׂ֔ים\rb* \rb Are you|אַתֶּ֥ם\rb* \rb rebelling|מֹרְדִֽים׃\rb* \rb against|הַעַ֥ל\rb* \rb the king?”|הַמֶּ֖לֶךְ\rb*
\p \v 20 \rb So I answered|וָאָשִׁ֨יב\rb* \rb them|אוֹתָ֜ם\rb* \rb and said,|וָאוֹמַ֤ר\rb*\rb |לָהֶם֙\rb* \rb “The God|אֱלֹהֵ֣י\rb* \rb of heaven|הַשָּׁמַ֔יִם\rb* \rb is the One|ה֚וּא\rb* \rb who will grant us success.|יַצְלִ֣יחַֽ\rb* \rb We,|וַאֲנַ֥חְנוּ\rb* \rb His servants,|עֲבָדָ֖יו\rb* \rb will start|נָק֣וּם\rb* \rb rebuilding,|וּבָנִ֑ינוּ\rb* \rb but you|וְלָכֶ֗ם\rb* \rb have no|אֵֽין־\rb* \rb portion,|חֵ֧לֶק\rb* \rb right,|וּצְדָקָ֛ה\rb* \rb or claim|וְזִכָּר֖וֹן\rb* \rb in Jerusalem.”|בִּירוּשָׁלִָֽם׃\rb*
\c 3
\s1 The Builders of the Walls
