\s1 The Work Ridiculed
\p \v 1 \rb Now|וַיְהִ֞י\rb* \rb when|כַּאֲשֶׁ֧ר\rb* \rb Sanballat|סַנְבַלַּ֗ט\rb* \rb heard|שָׁמַ֣ע\rb* \rb that|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb we|אֲנַ֤חְנוּ\rb* \rb were rebuilding|בוֹנִים֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the wall,|הַ֣חוֹמָ֔ה\rb* \rb he was furious|וַיִּ֣חַר\rb* \rb and filled with indignation.|וַיִּכְעַ֖ס\rb*\rb |הַרְבֵּ֑ה\rb* \rb He ridiculed|וַיַּלְעֵ֖ג\rb*\rb |עַל־\rb* \rb the Jews|הַיְּהוּדִֽים׃\rb* \v 2 \rb before|לִפְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb his associates|אֶחָ֗יו\rb* \rb and the army|וְחֵיל֙\rb* \rb of Samaria,|שֹֽׁמְר֔וֹן\rb*\rb |וַיֹּ֕אמֶר\rb* \rb saying,|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר׀\rb* \rb “What|מָ֛ה\rb* \rb are these feeble|הָאֲמֵלָלִ֖ים\rb* \rb Jews|הַיְּהוּדִ֥ים\rb* \rb doing?|עֹשִׂ֑ים\rb* \rb Can they restore the wall|הֲיַעַזְב֨וּ\rb* \rb by themselves?|לָהֶ֤ם\rb*\f + \fr 4:2 \ft Or \fqa Will they commit themselves to God?\f* \rb Will they offer sacrifices?|הֲיִזְבָּ֙חוּ֙\rb* \rb Will they complete it|הַיְכַלּ֣וּ\rb* \rb in a day?|בַיּ֔וֹם\rb* \rb Can they bring these|וְהֵ֥מָּה\rb* \rb burnt|שְׂרוּפֽוֹת׃\rb* \rb stones|הָאֲבָנִ֛ים\rb* \rb back to life|הַיְחַיּ֧וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb from the mounds|מֵעֲרֵמ֥וֹת\rb* \rb of rubble?”|הֶעָפָ֖ר\rb*
\p \v 3 \rb Then Tobiah|וְטוֹבִיָּ֥ה\rb* \rb the Ammonite,|הָעַמֹּנִ֖י\rb* \rb who was beside him,|אֶצְל֑וֹ\rb* \rb said,|וַיֹּ֗אמֶר\rb* \rb “If|אִם־\rb* \rb even|גַּ֚ם\rb* \rb a fox|שׁוּעָ֔ל\rb* \rb were to climb up on|יַעֲלֶ֣ה\rb* \rb what|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb they|הֵ֣ם\rb* \rb are building,|בּוֹנִ֔ים\rb* \rb it would break down|וּפָרַ֖ץ\rb* \rb their wall|חוֹמַ֥ת\rb* \rb of stones!”|אַבְנֵיהֶֽם׃פ\rb*
\p \v 4 \rb Hear us,|שְׁמַ֤ע\rb* \rb O God,|אֱלֹהֵ֙ינוּ֙\rb* \rb for|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb we are|הָיִ֣ינוּ\rb* \rb despised.|בוּזָ֔ה\rb* \rb Turn|וְהָשֵׁ֥ב\rb* \rb their scorn|חֶרְפָּתָ֖ם\rb* \rb back upon|אֶל־\rb* \rb their own heads,|רֹאשָׁ֑ם\rb* \rb and let them be taken|וּתְנֵ֥ם\rb* \rb as plunder|לְבִזָּ֖ה\rb* \rb to a land|בְּאֶ֥רֶץ\rb* \rb of captivity.|שִׁבְיָֽה׃\rb* \v 5 \rb Do not|וְאַל־\rb* \rb cover up|תְּכַס֙\rb*\rb |עַל־\rb* \rb their iniquity|עֲוֺנָ֔ם\rb* \rb or let their sin|וְחַטָּאתָ֖ם\rb* \rb be blotted out|תִּמָּחֶ֑ה\rb* \rb from Your sight,|מִלְּפָנֶ֣יךָ\rb*\rb |אַל־\rb* \rb for|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb they have provoked|הִכְעִ֖יסוּ\rb*\rb |לְנֶ֥גֶד\rb* \rb the builders.|הַבּוֹנִֽים׃\rb*\f + \fr 4:5 \ft Or \fqa have provoked You to anger before the builders\f*
\p \v 6 \rb So we rebuilt|וַנִּבְנֶה֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the wall|הַ֣חוֹמָ֔ה\rb* \rb until all|כָּל־\rb* \rb of it|הַחוֹמָ֖ה\rb* \rb was joined together|וַתִּקָּשֵׁ֥ר\rb* \rb up to|עַד־\rb* \rb half its height,|חֶצְיָ֑הּ\rb* \rb for the people|לָעָ֖ם\rb* \rb had|וַיְהִ֧י\rb* \rb a mind|לֵ֦ב\rb* \rb to work.|לַעֲשֽׂוֹת׃פ\rb*
\p \v 7 \rb |וַיְהִ֣י\rb* \rb When|כַאֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb Sanballat|סַנְבַלַּ֡ט\rb* \rb and Tobiah,|וְ֠טוֹבִיָּה\rb* \rb together with the Arabs,|וְהָעַרְבִ֨ים\rb* \rb Ammonites,|וְהָעַמֹּנִ֜ים\rb* \rb and Ashdodites,|וְהָאַשְׁדּוֹדִ֗ים\rb* \rb heard|שָׁמַ֣ע\rb* \rb that|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb the repair|אֲרוּכָה֙\rb* \rb to the walls|לְחֹמ֣וֹת\rb* \rb of Jerusalem|יְרוּשָׁלִַ֔ם\rb* \rb was progressing|עָלְתָ֤ה\rb* \rb and that|כִּי־\rb*\rb |הֵחֵ֥לּוּ\rb* \rb the gaps|הַפְּרֻצִ֖ים\rb* \rb were being closed,|לְהִסָּתֵ֑ם\rb* \rb they were furious,|וַיִּ֥חַר\rb*\rb |מְאֹֽד׃\rb* \v 8 \rb and all of them|כֻלָּם֙\rb* \rb conspired|וַיִּקְשְׁר֤וּ\rb*\rb |יַחְדָּ֔ו\rb* \rb to come|לָב֖וֹא\rb* \rb and fight|לְהִלָּחֵ֣ם\rb* \rb against Jerusalem|בִּירוּשָׁלִָ֑ם\rb* \rb and create|וְלַעֲשׂ֥וֹת\rb* \rb a hindrance.|תּוֹעָֽה׃\rb*
\s1 Discouragement Overcome
\p \v 9 \rb So we prayed|וַנִּתְפַּלֵּ֖ל\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb our God|אֱלֹהֵ֑ינוּ\rb* \rb and posted|וַנַּעֲמִ֨יד\rb* \rb a guard|מִשְׁמָ֧ר\rb* \rb against them|עֲלֵיהֶ֛ם\rb*\rb |מִפְּנֵיהֶֽם׃\rb* \rb day|יוֹמָ֥ם\rb* \rb and night.|וָלַ֖יְלָה\rb*
\p \v 10 \rb Meanwhile, the people of Judah|יְהוּדָ֗ה\rb* \rb said:|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb*\f + \fr 4:10 \ft Or \fqa Meanwhile, Judah said\f*
