\q1 \rb that we|וַאֲנַ֙חְנוּ֙\rb* \rb will never|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb be able|נוּכַ֔ל\rb*
\q2 \rb to rebuild|לִבְנ֖וֹת\rb* \rb the wall.”|בַּחוֹמָֽה׃\rb*
\p \v 11 \rb And our enemies|צָרֵ֗ינוּ\rb* \rb said,|וַיֹּאמְר֣וּ\rb* \rb “Before|עַ֛ד\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb they know|יֵדְעוּ֙\rb* \rb or|וְלֹ֣א\rb* \rb see|יִרְא֔וּ\rb* \rb a thing,|לֹ֤א\rb* \rb we will come|נָב֥וֹא\rb* \rb into|אֶל־\rb* \rb their midst,|תּוֹכָ֖ם\rb* \rb kill them,|וַהֲרַגְנ֑וּם\rb* \rb and put an end|וְהִשְׁבַּ֖תְנוּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb to the work.”|הַמְּלָאכָֽה׃\rb*
\p \v 12 \rb At that time|וַֽיְהִי֙\rb*\rb |כַּאֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb the Jews|הַיְּהוּדִ֔ים\rb* \rb who lived|הַיֹּשְׁבִ֖ים\rb* \rb nearby|אֶצְלָ֑ם\rb* \rb came|בָּ֣אוּ\rb* \rb and told|וַיֹּ֤אמְרוּ\rb* \rb us|לָ֙נוּ֙\rb* \rb ten|עֶ֣שֶׂר\rb* \rb times over,|פְּעָמִ֔ים\rb* \rb “Wherever|מִכָּל־\rb*\rb |הַמְּקֹמ֖וֹת\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb you turn,|תָּשׁ֥וּבוּ\rb* \rb they will attack us.”|עָלֵֽינוּ׃\rb*
\p \v 13 \rb So I stationed men|וָֽאַעֲמִ֞יד\rb* \rb behind|מֵאַחֲרֵ֥י\rb* \rb the lowest|מִֽתַּחְתִּיּ֧וֹת\rb* \rb sections|לַמָּק֛וֹם\rb* \rb of the wall,|לַחוֹמָ֖ה\rb* \rb at the vulnerable areas.|בַּצְּחִחִיִּים\rb* \rb I stationed|וָֽאַעֲמִ֤יד\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb them|הָעָם֙\rb* \rb by families|לְמִשְׁפָּח֔וֹת\rb* \rb with|עִם־\rb* \rb their swords,|חַרְבֹתֵיהֶ֛ם\rb* \rb spears,|רָמְחֵיהֶ֖ם\rb* \rb and bows.|וְקַשְּׁתֹתֵיהֶֽם׃\rb*
\p \v 14 \rb After I had made an inspection,|וָאֵ֣רֶא\rb* \rb I stood up|וָאָק֗וּם\rb* \rb and said|וָאֹמַ֞ר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the nobles,|הַחֹרִ֤ים\rb*\rb |וְאֶל־\rb* \rb the officials,|הַסְּגָנִים֙\rb*\rb |וְאֶל־\rb* \rb and the rest|יֶ֣תֶר\rb* \rb of the people,|הָעָ֔ם\rb* \rb “Do not|אַל־\rb* \rb be afraid|תִּֽירְא֖וּ\rb* \rb of them.|מִפְּנֵיהֶ֑ם\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Remember|זְכֹ֔רוּ\rb* \rb the Lord,|אֲדֹנָ֞י\rb* \rb who is great|הַגָּד֤וֹל\rb* \rb and awesome,|וְהַנּוֹרָא֙\rb* \rb and fight|וְהִֽלָּחֲמ֗וּ\rb* \rb for|עַל־\rb* \rb your brothers,|אֲחֵיכֶם֙\rb* \rb your sons|בְּנֵיכֶ֣ם\rb* \rb and your daughters,|וּבְנֹתֵיכֶ֔ם\rb* \rb your wives|נְשֵׁיכֶ֖ם\rb* \rb and your homes.”|וּבָתֵּיכֶֽם׃פ\rb*
\p \v 15 \rb |וַיְהִ֞י\rb* \rb When|כַּֽאֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb our enemies|אוֹיְבֵ֙ינוּ֙\rb* \rb heard|שָׁמְע֤וּ\rb* \rb that|כִּי־\rb* \rb we were aware|נ֣וֹדַֽע\rb* \rb of their scheme|עֲצָתָ֑ם\rb* \rb and that God|הָאֱלֹהִ֖ים\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb had frustrated it,|וַיָּ֥פֶר\rb* \rb each|כֻּלָּ֙נוּ֙\rb* \rb of us returned|וַנָּשׁוּב\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb his own|אִ֖ישׁ\rb* \rb work|מְלַאכְתּֽוֹ׃\rb* \rb on|אֶל־\rb* \rb the wall.|הַ֣חוֹמָ֔ה\rb* \v 16 \rb And|וַיְהִ֣י׀\rb* \rb from|מִן־\rb* \rb that|הַה֗וּא\rb* \rb day on,|הַיּ֣וֹם\rb* \rb half|חֲצִ֣י\rb* \rb of my servants|נְעָרַי֮\rb* \rb did|עֹשִׂ֣ים\rb* \rb the work|בַּמְּלָאכָה֒\rb* \rb while the other half|וְחֶצְיָ֗ם\rb* \rb held|מַחֲזִיקִים֙\rb* \rb spears,|וְהָרְמָחִ֣ים\rb* \rb shields,|הַמָּגִנִּ֔ים\rb* \rb bows,|וְהַקְּשָׁת֖וֹת\rb* \rb and armor.|וְהַשִּׁרְיֹנִ֑ים\rb*
\p \rb The officers|וְהַ֨שָּׂרִ֔ים\rb* \rb stationed themselves behind|אַחֲרֵ֖י\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the people|בֵּ֥ית\rb* \rb of Judah|יְהוּדָֽה׃\rb* \v 17 \rb who were rebuilding|הַבּוֹנִ֧ים\rb* \rb the wall.|בַּחוֹמָ֛ה\rb* \rb The laborers who carried|וְהַנֹּשְׂאִ֥ים\rb* \rb materials|בַּסֶּ֖בֶל\rb*\rb |עֹמְשִׂ֑ים\rb* \rb worked|עֹשֶׂ֣ה\rb*\rb |בַמְּלָאכָ֔ה\rb* \rb with one|בְּאַחַ֤ת\rb* \rb hand|יָדוֹ֙\rb* \rb and held|מַחֲזֶ֥קֶת\rb* \rb a weapon|הַשָּֽׁלַח׃\rb* \rb with the other.|וְאַחַ֖ת\rb* \v 18 \rb And each|אִ֥ישׁ\rb* \rb of the builders|וְהַ֨בּוֹנִ֔ים\rb* \rb worked|וּבוֹנִ֑ים\rb* \rb with his sword|חַרְבּ֛וֹ\rb* \rb strapped|אֲסוּרִ֥ים\rb* \rb at|עַל־\rb* \rb his side.|מָתְנָ֖יו\rb* \rb But the trumpeter|וְהַתּוֹקֵ֥עַ\rb*\rb |בַּשּׁוֹפָ֖ר\rb* \rb stayed beside me.|אֶצְלִֽי׃\rb*
\p \v 19 \rb Then I said|וָאֹמַ֞ר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the nobles,|הַחֹרִ֤ים\rb*\rb |וְאֶל־\rb* \rb the officials,|הַסְּגָנִים֙\rb*\rb |וְאֶל־\rb* \rb and the rest|יֶ֣תֶר\rb* \rb of the people:|הָעָ֔ם\rb* \rb “The work is|הַמְּלָאכָ֥ה\rb* \rb great|הַרְבֵּ֖ה\rb* \rb and extensive,|וּרְחָבָ֑ה\rb* \rb and we|וַאֲנַ֗חְנוּ\rb* \rb are spread out|נִפְרָדִים֙\rb* \rb far|רְחוֹקִ֖ים\rb* \rb from one|אִ֥ישׁ\rb* \rb another|מֵאָחִֽיו׃\rb* \rb along|עַל־\rb* \rb the wall.|הַ֣חוֹמָ֔ה\rb* \v 20 \rb Wherever|בִּמְק֗וֹם\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֤ר\rb* \rb you hear|תִּשְׁמְעוּ֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the sound|ק֣וֹל\rb* \rb of the horn,|הַשּׁוֹפָ֔ר\rb* \rb rally|תִּקָּבְצ֣וּ\rb* \rb to us|אֵלֵ֑ינוּ\rb* \rb there.|שָׁ֖מָּה\rb* \rb Our God|אֱלֹהֵ֖ינוּ\rb* \rb will fight|יִלָּ֥חֶם\rb* \rb for us!”|לָֽנוּ׃\rb*
\p \v 21 \rb So we|וַאֲנַ֖חְנוּ\rb* \rb continued|עֹשִׂ֣ים\rb* \rb the work,|בַּמְּלָאכָ֑ה\rb* \rb while half of the men|וְחֶצְיָ֗ם\rb* \rb held|מַחֲזִיקִים֙\rb* \rb spears|בָּֽרְמָחִ֔ים\rb* \rb from the break|מֵעֲל֣וֹת\rb* \rb of dawn|הַשַּׁ֔חַר\rb* \rb until|עַ֖ד\rb* \rb the stars|הַכּוֹכָבִֽים׃\rb* \rb came out.|צֵ֥את\rb* \v 22 \rb At that|הַהִיא֙\rb* \rb time|בָּעֵ֤ת\rb* \rb I also|גַּ֣ם\rb* \rb said|אָמַ֣רְתִּי\rb* \rb to the people,|לָעָ֔ם\rb* \rb “Let every man|אִ֣ישׁ\rb* \rb and his servant|וְנַעֲר֔וֹ\rb* \rb spend the night|יָלִ֖ינוּ\rb* \rb inside|בְּת֣וֹךְ\rb* \rb Jerusalem,|יְרוּשָׁלִָ֑ם\rb* \rb so that they can stand|וְהָֽיוּ־\rb* \rb guard|מִשְׁמָ֖ר\rb* \rb by night|הַלַּ֛יְלָה\rb* \rb and work|מְלָאכָֽה׃\rb* \rb by day.”|וְהַיּ֥וֹם\rb*
\p \v 23 \rb So neither I|אֲנִ֜י\rb*\rb |וְאֵ֨ין\rb* \rb nor my brothers|וְאַחַ֣י\rb* \rb nor my servants|וּנְעָרַ֗י\rb*\rb |וְאַנְשֵׁ֤י\rb* \rb nor the guards|הַמִּשְׁמָר֙\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb with me|אַחֲרַ֔י\rb*\rb |אֵין־\rb*\rb |אֲנַ֥חְנוּ\rb* \rb changed out of|פֹשְׁטִ֖ים\rb* \rb our clothes;|בְּגָדֵ֑ינוּ\rb* \rb each|אִ֖ישׁ\rb* \rb carried his weapon,|שִׁלְח֥וֹ\rb* \rb even to go for water.|הַמָּֽיִם׃ס\rb*\f + \fr 4:23 \ft Or \fqa each carried his weapon in his right hand\f*
\c 5
\s1 Nehemiah Defends the Oppressed
\p \v 1 \rb About that time there was|וַתְּהִ֨י\rb* \rb a great|גְּדוֹלָ֑ה\rb* \rb outcry|צַעֲקַ֥ת\rb* \rb from the people|הָעָ֛ם\rb* \rb and their wives|וּנְשֵׁיהֶ֖ם\rb* \rb against|אֶל־\rb* \rb their fellow|אֲחֵיהֶ֖ם\rb* \rb Jews.|הַיְּהוּדִֽים׃\rb*
\p \v 2 \rb |וְיֵשׁ֙\rb* \rb Some|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb were saying,|אֹמְרִ֔ים\rb* \rb “We|אֲנַ֣חְנוּ\rb* \rb and our sons|בָּנֵ֥ינוּ\rb* \rb and daughters|וּבְנֹתֵ֖ינוּ\rb* \rb are numerous.|רַבִּ֑ים\rb* \rb We must get|וְנִקְחָ֥ה\rb* \rb grain|דָגָ֖ן\rb* \rb in order to eat|וְנֹאכְלָ֥ה\rb* \rb and stay alive.”|וְנִחְיֶֽה׃\rb*
\p \v 3 \rb |וְיֵשׁ֙\rb* \rb Others|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb were saying,|אֹמְרִ֔ים\rb* \rb “We|אֲנַ֣חְנוּ\rb* \rb are mortgaging|עֹרְבִ֑ים\rb* \rb our fields,|שְׂדֹתֵ֛ינוּ\rb* \rb our vineyards,|וּכְרָמֵ֥ינוּ\rb* \rb and our homes|וּבָתֵּ֖ינוּ\rb* \rb to get|וְנִקְחָ֥ה\rb* \rb grain|דָגָ֖ן\rb* \rb during the famine.”|בָּרָעָֽב׃\rb*
\p \v 4 \rb |וְיֵשׁ֙\rb* \rb Still others|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb were saying,|אֹמְרִ֔ים\rb* \rb “We have borrowed|לָוִ֥ינוּ\rb* \rb money to pay|כֶ֖סֶף\rb* \rb the king’s|הַמֶּ֑לֶךְ\rb* \rb tax|לְמִדַּ֣ת\rb* \rb on our fields|שְׂדֹתֵ֖ינוּ\rb* \rb and vineyards.|וּכְרָמֵֽינוּ׃\rb* \v 5 \rb |וְעַתָּ֗ה\rb*\rb |כִּבְשַׂ֤ר\rb* \rb We and our children|כִּבְנֵיהֶ֖ם\rb* \rb are just like our countrymen|אַחֵ֙ינוּ֙\rb*\rb |בְּשָׂרֵ֔נוּ\rb* \rb and their children,|בָּנֵ֑ינוּ\rb*\rb |וְהִנֵּ֣ה\rb* \rb yet we|אֲנַ֣חְנוּ\rb* \rb are subjecting|כֹ֠בְשִׁים\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb our sons|בָּנֵ֨ינוּ\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and daughters|בְּנֹתֵ֜ינוּ\rb* \rb to slavery.|לַעֲבָדִ֗ים\rb* \rb Some of|וְיֵ֨שׁ\rb* \rb our daughters|מִבְּנֹתֵ֤ינוּ\rb* \rb are already enslaved,|נִכְבָּשׁוֹת֙\rb* \rb but we are powerless to redeem them|וְאֵ֣ין\rb*\rb |לְאֵ֣ל\rb*\rb |יָדֵ֔נוּ\rb* \rb because our fields|וּשְׂדֹתֵ֥ינוּ\rb* \rb and vineyards|וּכְרָמֵ֖ינוּ\rb* \rb belong to others.”|לַאֲחֵרִֽים׃\rb*
\p \v 6 \rb When|כַּאֲשֶׁ֤ר\rb* \rb I heard|שָׁמַ֙עְתִּי֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb their outcry|זַֽעֲקָתָ֔ם\rb*\rb |וְאֵ֖ת\rb* \rb and these|הָאֵֽלֶּה׃\rb* \rb complaints,|הַדְּבָרִ֥ים\rb* \rb I became extremely|מְאֹ֑ד\rb* \rb angry,|וַיִּ֥חַר\rb* \v 7 \rb and after serious|לִבִּ֜י\rb* \rb thought|וַיִּמָּלֵ֨ךְ\rb* \rb I rebuked|וָאָרִ֙יבָה֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the nobles|הַחֹרִ֣ים\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and officials,|הַסְּגָנִ֔ים\rb* \rb saying,|וָאֹמְרָ֣ה\rb* \rb |אִישׁ־\rb* \rb “You|אַתֶּ֣ם\rb* \rb are exacting|נֹשִׁ֑אים\rb* \rb usury|מַשָּׁ֥א\rb* \rb from your own brothers!”|בְּאָחִ֖יו\rb*
\p \rb So I called|וָאֶתֵּ֥ן\rb* \rb a large|גְדוֹלָֽה׃\rb* \rb assembly|קְהִלָּ֥ה\rb* \rb against them|עֲלֵיהֶ֖ם\rb* \v 8 \rb and said,|וָאֹמְרָ֣ה\rb* \rb “We|אֲנַ֣חְנוּ\rb* \rb have done our best|כְּדֵ֣י\rb*\rb |וְגַם־\rb* \rb to buy back|קָ֠נִינוּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb our Jewish|הַיְּהוּדִ֜ים\rb* \rb brothers|אַחֵ֨ינוּ\rb* \rb who were sold|הַנִּמְכָּרִ֤ים\rb* \rb to foreigners,|לַגּוֹיִם֙\rb* \rb but now you|אַתֶּ֛ם\rb* \rb are selling|תִּמְכְּר֥וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb your own brothers,|אֲחֵיכֶ֖ם\rb* \rb that they may be sold back|וְנִמְכְּרוּ־\rb* \rb to us!”|לָ֑נוּ\rb*
\p \rb But they remained silent,|וַֽיַּחֲרִ֔ישׁוּ\rb* \rb for they could find|מָצְא֖וּ\rb* \rb nothing|וְלֹ֥א\rb* \rb to say.|דָּבָֽר׃ס\rb*
\p \v 9 \rb So I continued,|וַיֹּאמֶר\rb* \rb “What|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb you|אַתֶּ֣ם\rb* \rb are doing|עֹשִׂ֑ים\rb* \rb is not|לֹא־\rb* \rb right.|ט֥וֹב\rb*\rb |הַדָּבָ֖ר\rb* \rb Shouldn’t|הֲל֞וֹא\rb* \rb you walk|תֵּלֵ֔כוּ\rb* \rb in the fear|בְּיִרְאַ֤ת\rb* \rb of our God|אֱלֹהֵ֙ינוּ֙\rb* \rb to avoid the reproach|מֵחֶרְפַּ֖ת\rb* \rb of our foreign|הַגּוֹיִ֥ם\rb* \rb enemies?|אוֹיְבֵֽינוּ׃\rb* \v 10 \rb I,|אֲנִי֙\rb* \rb as well as|וְגַם־\rb* \rb my brothers|אַחַ֣י\rb* \rb and my servants,|וּנְעָרַ֔י\rb* \rb have been lending|נֹשִׁ֥ים\rb* \rb the people|בָּהֶ֖ם\rb* \rb money|כֶּ֣סֶף\rb* \rb and grain.|וְדָגָ֑ן\rb* \rb Please,|נָּ֖א\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb let us stop|נַֽעַזְבָה־\rb* \rb this|הַזֶּֽה׃\rb* \rb usury.|הַמַּשָּׁ֥א\rb* \v 11 \rb Please|נָ֨א\rb* \rb restore|הָשִׁיבוּ֩\rb* \rb to them|לָהֶ֜ם\rb* \rb immediately|כְּהַיּ֗וֹם\rb* \rb their fields,|שְׂדֹתֵיהֶ֛ם\rb* \rb vineyards,|כַּרְמֵיהֶ֥ם\rb* \rb olive groves,|זֵיתֵיהֶ֖ם\rb* \rb and houses,|וּבָתֵּיהֶ֑ם\rb* \rb along with the percentage|וּמְאַ֨ת\rb* \rb of the money,|הַכֶּ֤סֶף\rb* \rb grain,|וְהַדָּגָן֙\rb* \rb new wine,|הַתִּיר֣וֹשׁ\rb* \rb and oil|וְהַיִּצְהָ֔ר\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb you|אַתֶּ֖ם\rb* \rb have been assessing|נֹשִׁ֥ים\rb* \rb them.”|בָּהֶֽם׃\rb*
\p \v 12 \rb “We will restore it,”|נָשִׁ֗יב\rb* \rb they replied,|וַיֹּאמְר֣וּ\rb* \rb “and will require|נְבַקֵּ֔שׁ\rb*\rb |כֵּ֣ן\rb* \rb nothing|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb more from them.|וּמֵהֶם֙\rb* \rb We will do|נַעֲשֶׂ֔ה\rb* \rb as|כַּאֲשֶׁ֖ר\rb* \rb you|אַתָּ֣ה\rb* \rb say.”|אוֹמֵ֑ר\rb*
\p \rb So I summoned|וָאֶקְרָא֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the priests|הַכֹּ֣הֲנִ֔ים\rb* \rb and required of the nobles and officials an oath that they|וָֽאַשְׁבִּיעֵ֔ם\rb* \rb would do|לַעֲשׂ֖וֹת\rb* \rb what they had promised.|כַּדָּבָ֥ר\rb*\rb |הַזֶּֽה׃\rb* \v 13 \rb I also|גַּם־\rb* \rb shook out|נָעַ֗רְתִּי\rb* \rb the folds of my robe|חָצְנִ֣י\rb* \rb and said,|וָֽאֹמְרָ֡ה\rb* \rb “May God|הָֽאֱלֹהִ֟ים\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb likewise|כָּ֣כָה\rb* \rb shake|יְנַעֵ֪ר\rb* \rb out of his house|מִבֵּיתוֹ֙\rb* \rb and possessions|וּמִ֣יגִיע֔וֹ\rb*\rb |וְכָ֛כָה\rb* \rb every|כָּל־\rb* \rb man|הָאִישׁ֩\rb* \rb who|אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb does not|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb keep|יָקִ֜ים\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb this|הַזֶּ֗ה\rb* \rb promise.|הַדָּבָ֣ר\rb* \rb May such a man be|יִהְיֶ֥ה\rb* \rb shaken out|נָע֖וּר\rb* \rb and have nothing!”|וָרֵ֑ק\rb*
\p \rb The whole|כָֽל־\rb* \rb assembly|הַקָּהָ֜ל\rb* \rb said,|וַיֹּאמְר֨וּ\rb* \rb “Amen,”|אָמֵ֗ן\rb* \rb and they praised|וַֽיְהַלְלוּ֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the LORD.|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb And the people|הָעָ֖ם\rb* \rb did|וַיַּ֥עַשׂ\rb* \rb as they had promised.|כַּדָּבָ֥ר\rb*\rb |הַזֶּֽה׃\rb*
\s1 Nehemiah’s Generosity
\p \v 14 \rb Furthermore,|גַּ֞ם\rb* \rb from the day|מִיּ֣וֹם׀\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb King|הַמֶּ֔לֶךְ\rb* \rb Artaxerxes|לְאַרְתַּחְשַׁ֣סְתְּא\rb* \rb appointed me|צִוָּ֣ה\rb*\rb |אֹתִ֗י\rb* \rb to be|לִהְי֣וֹת\rb* \rb their governor|פֶּחָם֮\rb* \rb in the land|בְּאֶ֣רֶץ\rb* \rb of Judah,|יְהוּדָה֒\rb* \rb from his twentieth|עֶשְׂרִ֗ים\rb* \rb year|מִשְּׁנַ֣ת\rb* \rb until|וְ֠עַד\rb* \rb his thirty-second|שְׁלֹשִׁ֤ים\rb*\rb |וּשְׁתַּ֙יִם֙\rb* \rb year|שְׁנַ֨ת\rb* \rb (twelve|שְׁתֵּ֣ים\rb*\rb |עֶשְׂרֵ֑ה\rb* \rb years total),|שָׁנִ֖ים\rb* \rb neither I|אֲנִ֣י\rb* \rb nor my brothers|וְאַחַ֔י\rb*\rb |לֹ֥א\rb* \rb ate|אָכַֽלְתִּי׃\rb* \rb the food|לֶ֥חֶם\rb* \rb allotted to the governor.|הַפֶּ֖חָה\rb*
\p \v 15 \rb The governors|וְהַפַּחוֹת֩\rb*\rb |הָרִאשֹׁנִ֨ים\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb before me|לְפָנַ֜י\rb* \rb had heavily burdened|הִכְבִּ֣ידוּ\rb*\rb |עַל־\rb* \rb the people,|הָעָ֗ם\rb* \rb taking|וַיִּקְח֨וּ\rb* \rb from them|מֵהֶ֜ם\rb* \rb bread|בְּלֶ֤חֶם\rb* \rb and wine|וָיַ֙יִן֙\rb* \rb plus|אַחַר֙\rb* \rb forty|אַרְבָּעִ֔ים\rb* \rb shekels|שְׁקָלִ֣ים\rb* \rb of silver.|כֶּֽסֶף־\rb*\f + \fr 5:15 \fqa 40 shekels \ft is approximately 1 pound or 453.6 grams of silver.\f* \rb Their servants|נַעֲרֵיהֶ֖ם\rb* \rb also|גַּ֥ם\rb* \rb oppressed|שָׁלְט֣וּ\rb*\rb |עַל־\rb* \rb the people.|הָעָ֑ם\rb* \rb But I|וַאֲנִי֙\rb* \rb did not|לֹא־\rb* \rb do|עָשִׂ֣יתִי\rb* \rb this,|כֵ֔ן\rb* \rb because|מִפְּנֵ֖י\rb* \rb of my fear|יִרְאַ֥ת\rb* \rb of God.|אֱלֹהִֽים׃\rb* \v 16 \rb Instead,|וְ֠גַם\rb* \rb I devoted myself|הֶחֱזַ֔קְתִּי\rb* \rb to the construction|בִּמְלֶ֜אכֶת\rb* \rb of the|הַזֹּאת֙\rb* \rb wall,|הַחוֹמָ֤ה\rb* \rb and all|וְכָל־\rb* \rb my servants|נְעָרַ֔י\rb* \rb were gathered|קְבוּצִ֥ים\rb* \rb there|שָׁ֖ם\rb* \rb for|עַל־\rb* \rb the work;|הַמְּלָאכָֽה׃\rb* \rb we did not|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb acquire|קָנִ֑ינוּ\rb* \rb any land.|וְשָׂדֶ֖ה\rb*
\p \v 17 \rb There were 150|מֵאָ֧ה\rb*\rb |וַחֲמִשִּׁ֣ים\rb*\rb |אִ֗ישׁ\rb* \rb Jews|וְהַיְּהוּדִ֨ים\rb* \rb and officials|וְהַסְּגָנִ֜ים\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb at|עַל־\rb* \rb my table,|שֻׁלְחָנִֽי׃\rb* \rb besides the guests|וְהַבָּאִ֥ים\rb*\rb |אֵלֵ֛ינוּ\rb* \rb from|מִן־\rb* \rb the surrounding|סְבִיבֹתֵ֖ינוּ\rb* \rb nations.|הַגּוֹיִ֥ם\rb* \v 18 \rb |וַאֲשֶׁר֩\rb*\rb |הָיָ֨ה\rb* \rb Each|אֶחָ֗ד\rb* \rb day|לְי֣וֹם\rb* \rb one|אֶחָ֞ד\rb* \rb ox,|שׁ֣וֹר\rb* \rb six|שֵׁשׁ־\rb* \rb choice|בְּרֻר֤וֹת\rb* \rb sheep,|צֹ֠אן\rb* \rb and some fowl|וְצִפֳּרִים֙\rb* \rb were prepared|נַֽעֲשׂוּ־\rb* \rb for me,|לִ֔י\rb* \rb and once every|וּבֵ֨ין\rb* \rb ten|עֲשֶׂ֧רֶת\rb* \rb days|יָמִ֛ים\rb* \rb an abundance|לְהַרְבֵּ֑ה\rb*\rb |וְעִם־\rb* \rb of all kinds|בְּכָל־\rb* \rb of wine was provided.|יַ֖יִן\rb* \rb But I did not|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb demand|בִקַּ֔שְׁתִּי\rb* \rb the food|לֶ֤חֶם\rb* \rb allotted to the governor,|הַפֶּחָה֙\rb* \rb because|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb the burden|הָעֲבֹדָ֖ה\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb the people|הָעָ֥ם\rb*\rb |הַזֶּֽה׃\rb* \rb was so heavy.|כָֽבְדָ֥ה\rb*
\p \v 19 \rb Remember|זָכְרָה־\rb* \rb me|לִּ֥י\rb* \rb favorably,|לְטוֹבָ֑ה\rb* \rb O my God,|אֱלֹהַ֖י\rb* \rb for all|כֹּ֥ל\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb I have done|עָשִׂ֖יתִי\rb* \rb for|עַל־\rb* \rb this|הַזֶּֽה׃פ\rb* \rb people.|הָעָ֥ם\rb*
\c 6
\s1 Sanballat’s Conspiracy
\p \v 1 \rb |וַיְהִ֣י\rb* \rb When|כַאֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb Sanballat,|לְסַנְבַלַּ֣ט\rb* \rb Tobiah,|וְ֠טוֹבִיָּה\rb* \rb Geshem|וּלְגֶ֨שֶׁם\rb* \rb the Arab,|הָֽעַרְבִ֜י\rb* \rb and the rest|וּלְיֶ֣תֶר\rb* \rb of our enemies|אֹֽיְבֵ֗ינוּ\rb* \rb heard|נִשְׁמַ֣ע\rb* \rb that|כִּ֤י\rb* \rb I had rebuilt|בָנִ֙יתִי֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the wall|הַ֣חוֹמָ֔ה\rb* \rb and not|וְלֹא־\rb* \rb a gap|פָּ֑רֶץ\rb* \rb was left—|נ֥וֹתַר\rb* \rb though|גַּ֚ם\rb* \rb to|עַד־\rb* \rb that|הַהִ֔יא\rb* \rb time|הָעֵ֣ת\rb* \rb I had not yet|לֹא־\rb* \rb installed|הֶעֱמַ֥דְתִּי\rb* \rb the doors|דְּלָת֖וֹת\rb* \rb in the gates—|בַשְּׁעָרִֽים׃\rb* \v 2 \rb Sanballat|סַנְבַלַּ֤ט\rb* \rb and Geshem|וְגֶ֙שֶׁם֙\rb*\rb |אֵלַ֣י\rb* \rb sent me|וַיִּשְׁלַ֨ח\rb* \rb this message:|לֵאמֹ֔ר\rb* \rb “Come,|לְכָ֞ה\rb* \rb let us meet|וְנִֽוָּעֲדָ֥ה\rb* \rb together|יַחְדָּ֛ו\rb* \rb in one of the villages|בַּכְּפִירִ֖ים\rb*\f + \fr 6:2 \ft Or \fqa in Kephirim\f* \rb on the plain|בְּבִקְעַ֣ת\rb*\f + \fr 6:2 \ft Or \fqa in the valley\f* \rb of Ono.”|אוֹנ֑וֹ\rb*
\p \rb But they|וְהֵ֙מָּה֙\rb* \rb were planning|חֹֽשְׁבִ֔ים\rb* \rb to harm|לַעֲשׂ֥וֹת\rb*\rb |רָעָֽה׃\rb* \rb me.|לִ֖י\rb*
\p \v 3 \rb So I sent|וָאֶשְׁלְחָ֨ה\rb* \rb messengers|מַלְאָכִים֙\rb* \rb to them,|עֲלֵיהֶ֤ם\rb* \rb saying,|לֵאמֹ֔ר\rb* \rb “I|אֲנִ֣י\rb* \rb am doing|עֹשֶׂ֔ה\rb* \rb a great|גְדוֹלָה֙\rb* \rb work|מְלָאכָ֤ה\rb* \rb and cannot|וְלֹ֥א\rb*\rb |אוּכַ֖ל\rb* \rb come down.|לָרֶ֑דֶת\rb* \rb Why|לָ֣מָּה\rb* \rb should the work|הַמְּלָאכָה֙\rb* \rb stop|תִשְׁבַּ֤ת\rb* \rb while|כַּאֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb I leave it|אַרְפֶּ֔הָ\rb* \rb to go down|וְיָרַדְתִּ֖י\rb* \rb to you?”|אֲלֵיכֶֽם׃\rb*
\p \v 4 \rb Four|אַרְבַּ֣ע\rb* \rb times|פְּעָמִ֑ים\rb* \rb they sent me|וַיִּשְׁלְח֥וּ\rb*\rb |אֵלַ֛י\rb* \rb the same|הַזֶּ֖ה\rb* \rb message,|כַּדָּבָ֥ר\rb* \rb and each time I gave|וָאָשִׁ֥יב\rb*\rb |אוֹתָ֖ם\rb* \rb the same|הַזֶּֽה׃ס\rb* \rb reply.|כַּדָּבָ֥ר\rb*
\p \v 5 \rb The fifth|חֲמִישִׁ֖ית\rb*\rb |אֶֽת־\rb* \rb time,|פַּ֥עַם\rb* \rb Sanballat|סַנְבַלַּ֜ט\rb* \rb sent me|וַיִּשְׁלַח֩\rb*\rb |אֵלַ֨י\rb* \rb this|הַזֶּ֛ה\rb* \rb same message|כַּדָּבָ֥ר\rb* \rb by his young servant,|נַעֲר֑וֹ\rb* \rb who had in his hand|בְּיָדֽוֹ׃\rb* \rb an unsealed|פְּתוּחָ֖ה\rb* \rb letter|וְאִגֶּ֥רֶת\rb* \v 6 \rb that read:|כָּת֣וּב\rb*
\pmo \rb “It is reported|נִשְׁמָע֙\rb* \rb among the nations—|בַּגּוֹיִ֤ם\rb* \rb and Geshem|וְגַשְׁמ֣וּ\rb*\f + \fr 6:6 \ft Hebrew \fqa Gashmu\ft , a variant of \fqa Geshem\ft ; see verse 1.\f* \rb agrees—|אֹמֵ֔ר\rb* \rb that you|אַתָּ֤ה\rb* \rb and the Jews|וְהַיְּהוּדִים֙\rb* \rb are plotting|חֹשְׁבִ֣ים\rb* \rb to revolt,|לִמְר֔וֹד\rb* \rb and this is why|עַל־\rb*\rb |כֵּ֛ן\rb* \rb you|אַתָּ֥ה\rb* \rb are building|בוֹנֶ֖ה\rb* \rb the wall.|הַחוֹמָ֑ה\rb* \rb According to these|הָאֵֽלֶּה׃\rb* \rb reports,|כַּדְּבָרִ֖ים\rb* \rb you|וְאַתָּ֗ה\rb* \rb are to become|הֹוֶ֤ה\rb* \rb their|לָהֶם֙\rb* \rb king,|לְמֶ֔לֶךְ\rb* \v 7 \rb and you have even|וְגַם־\rb* \rb appointed|הֶעֱמַ֣דְתָּ\rb* \rb prophets|נְבִיאִ֡ים\rb* \rb in Jerusalem|בִֽירוּשָׁלִַ֜ם\rb*\rb |לֵאמֹ֗ר\rb* \rb to proclaim|לִקְרֹא֩\rb* \rb on your behalf:|עָלֶ֨יךָ\rb* \rb ‘There is a king|מֶ֚לֶךְ\rb* \rb in Judah.’|בִּֽיהוּדָ֔ה\rb* \rb Soon|וְעַתָּ֣ה\rb* \rb these|הָאֵ֑לֶּה\rb* \rb rumors|כַּדְּבָרִ֣ים\rb* \rb will reach the ears|יִשָּׁמַ֣ע\rb* \rb of the king.|לַמֶּ֔לֶךְ\rb* \rb So|וְעַתָּה֙\rb* \rb come,|לְכָ֔ה\rb* \rb let us confer|וְנִֽוָּעֲצָ֖ה\rb* \rb together.”|יַחְדָּֽו׃ס\rb*
\p \v 8 \rb Then I sent|וָאֶשְׁלְחָ֤ה\rb* \rb him|אֵלָיו֙\rb* \rb this reply:|לֵאמֹ֔ר\rb* \rb “There is|נִֽהְיָה֙\rb* \rb nothing|לֹ֤א\rb* \rb to these|הָאֵ֔לֶּה\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֖ר\rb* \rb rumors|כַּדְּבָרִ֣ים\rb* \rb you|אַתָּ֣ה\rb* \rb are spreading;|אוֹמֵ֑ר\rb*\rb |כִּ֥י\rb* \rb you|אַתָּ֥ה\rb* \rb are inventing them|בוֹדָֽאם׃\rb* \rb in your own mind.”|מִֽלִּבְּךָ֖\rb*
\p \v 9 \rb For|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb they were all|כֻלָּ֗ם\rb* \rb trying to frighten|מְיָֽרְאִ֤ים\rb* \rb us,|אוֹתָ֙נוּ֙\rb* \rb saying,|לֵאמֹ֔ר\rb* \rb “Their hands|יְדֵיהֶ֛ם\rb* \rb will be weakened|יִרְפּ֧וּ\rb* \rb in|מִן־\rb* \rb the work,|הַמְּלָאכָ֖ה\rb* \rb and it will never|וְלֹ֣א\rb* \rb be finished.”|תֵעָשֶׂ֑ה\rb*
\p \rb But now, my God,|וְעַתָּ֖ה\rb*\f + \fr 6:9 \ft Hebrew \fqa But now\ft ; for clarity, \fqa my God \ft has been included.\f* \rb strengthen|חַזֵּ֥ק\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb my hands.|יָדָֽי׃\rb*
\p \v 10 \rb Later, I|וַאֲנִי־\rb* \rb went|בָ֗אתִי\rb* \rb to the house|בֵּ֣ית\rb* \rb of Shemaiah|שְֽׁמַֽעְיָ֧ה\rb* \rb son|בֶן־\rb* \rb of Delaiah,|דְּלָיָ֛ה\rb* \rb the son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Mehetabel,|מְהֵֽיטַבְאֵ֖ל\rb* \rb who|וְה֣וּא\rb* \rb was confined|עָצ֑וּר\rb* \rb to his house. He said:|וַיֹּ֡אמֶר\rb*
\b 
\q1 \rb “Let us meet|נִוָּעֵד֩\rb* \rb at|אֶל־\rb* \rb the house|בֵּ֨ית\rb* \rb of God|הָאֱלֹהִ֜ים\rb*
\q2 \rb inside|אֶל־\rb*\rb |תּ֣וֹךְ\rb* \rb the temple.|הַֽהֵיכָ֗ל\rb*
\q1 \rb Let us shut|וְנִסְגְּרָה֙\rb* \rb the temple|הַהֵיכָ֔ל\rb* \rb doors|דַּלְת֣וֹת\rb*
\q2 \rb because|כִּ֚י\rb* \rb they are coming|בָּאִ֣ים\rb* \rb to kill you—|לְהָרְגֶ֔ךָ\rb*
\q2 \rb by night|וְלַ֖יְלָה\rb* \rb they are coming|בָּאִ֥ים\rb* \rb to kill you!”|לְהָרְגֶֽךָ׃\rb*
\p \v 11 \rb But I replied,|וָאֹמְרָ֗ה\rb* \rb “Should a man|הַאִ֤ישׁ\rb* \rb like me|כָּמ֙וֹנִי֙\rb* \rb run away?|יִבְרָ֔ח\rb* \rb Should|וּמִ֥י\rb* \rb one like me|כָמ֛וֹנִי\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb go|יָב֥וֹא\rb* \rb into|אֶל־\rb* \rb the temple|הַהֵיכָ֖ל\rb* \rb to save his own life?|וָחָ֑י\rb* \rb I will not|לֹ֖א\rb* \rb go!”|אָבֽוֹא׃\rb*
\p \v 12 \rb I realized|וָאַכִּ֕ירָה\rb*\rb |וְהִנֵּ֥ה\rb* \rb that God|אֱלֹהִ֖ים\rb* \rb had not|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb sent him,|שְׁלָח֑וֹ\rb* \rb but that he had uttered|דִּבֶּ֣ר\rb* \rb this prophecy|הַנְּבוּאָה֙\rb* \rb against me|עָלַ֔י\rb* \rb because|כִּ֤י\rb* \rb Tobiah|וְטוֹבִיָּ֥ה\rb* \rb and Sanballat|וְסַנְבַלַּ֖ט\rb* \rb had hired him.|שְׂכָרֽוֹ׃\rb* \v 13 \rb He|ה֔וּא\rb* \rb had been hired|שָׂכוּר֙\rb* \rb to|לְמַ֤עַן\rb* \rb intimidate me|אִירָ֥א\rb* \rb so that I would sin|וְחָטָ֑אתִי\rb* \rb by doing|וְאֶֽעֱשֶׂה־\rb* \rb as he suggested,|כֵּ֖ן\rb* \rb so they could give me|וְהָיָ֤ה\rb*\rb |לָהֶם֙\rb* \rb a bad|רָ֔ע\rb* \rb name|לְשֵׁ֣ם\rb* \rb in order to|לְמַ֖עַן\rb* \rb discredit me.|יְחָֽרְפֽוּנִי׃פ\rb*
\p \v 14 \rb O my God,|אֱלֹהַ֛י\rb* \rb remember|זָכְרָ֧ה\rb* \rb Tobiah|לְטוֹבִיָּ֥ה\rb* \rb and Sanballat|וּלְסַנְבַלַּ֖ט\rb* \rb for what they have done,|כְּמַעֲשָׂ֣יו\rb*\rb |אֵ֑לֶּה\rb* \rb and also|וְגַ֨ם\rb* \rb Noadiah|לְנוֹעַדְיָ֤ה\rb* \rb the prophetess|הַנְּבִיאָה֙\rb* \rb and the other|וּלְיֶ֣תֶר\rb* \rb prophets|הַנְּבִיאִ֔ים\rb* \rb who|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb*\rb |הָי֖וּ\rb* \rb tried to intimidate me.|מְיָֽרְאִ֥ים\rb*\rb |אוֹתִֽי׃\rb*
\s1 Completion of the Wall
\p \v 15 \rb So the wall|הַֽחוֹמָ֔ה\rb* \rb was completed|וַתִּשְׁלַם֙\rb* \rb in fifty-two|לַחֲמִשִּׁ֥ים\rb*\rb |וּשְׁנַ֖יִם\rb* \rb days,|יֽוֹם׃פ\rb* \rb on the twenty-fifth|בְּעֶשְׂרִ֥ים\rb*\rb |וַחֲמִשָּׁ֖ה\rb* \rb of Elul.|לֶאֱל֑וּל\rb*\f + \fr 6:15 \fqa Elul \ft is the sixth month of the Hebrew lunar calendar, usually occurring within the months of August and September.\f* \v 16 \rb |וַיְהִ֗י\rb* \rb When|כַּאֲשֶׁ֤ר\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb our enemies|א֣וֹיְבֵ֔ינוּ\rb*\rb |וַיִּֽרְא֗וּ\rb* \rb heard about this,|שָֽׁמְעוּ֙\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the surrounding|סְבִֽיבֹתֵ֔ינוּ\rb* \rb nations|הַגּוֹיִם֙\rb* \rb were afraid|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb and disheartened,|וַיִּפְּל֥וּ\rb*\rb |מְאֹ֖ד\rb*\rb |בְּעֵינֵיהֶ֑ם\rb* \rb for they realized|וַיֵּ֣דְע֔וּ\rb* \rb that|כִּ֚י\rb* \rb this|הַזֹּֽאת׃\rb* \rb task|הַמְּלָאכָ֥ה\rb* \rb had been accomplished|נֶעֶשְׂתָ֖ה\rb* \rb by|מֵאֵ֣ת\rb* \rb our God.|אֱלֹהֵ֔ינוּ\rb*
\p \v 17 \rb Also|גַּ֣ם׀\rb* \rb in those|הָהֵ֗ם\rb* \rb days,|בַּיָּמִ֣ים\rb* \rb the nobles|חֹרֵ֤י\rb* \rb of Judah|יְהוּדָה֙\rb* \rb sent many|מַרְבִּ֞ים\rb* \rb letters|אִגְּרֹ֣תֵיהֶ֔ם\rb*\rb |הוֹלְכ֖וֹת\rb* \rb to|עַל־\rb* \rb Tobiah,|טוֹבִיָּ֑ה\rb* \rb and Tobiah’s|לְטוֹבִיָּ֖ה\rb* \rb letters|וַאֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb kept coming|בָּא֥וֹת\rb* \rb to them.|אֲלֵיהֶֽם׃\rb* \v 18 \rb For|כִּי־\rb* \rb many|רַבִּ֣ים\rb* \rb in Judah|בִּֽיהוּדָ֗ה\rb* \rb were bound|בַּעֲלֵ֤י\rb* \rb by oath|שְׁבוּעָה֙\rb* \rb to him,|ל֔וֹ\rb* \rb since|כִּי־\rb* \rb he|ה֖וּא\rb* \rb was a son-in-law|חָתָ֥ן\rb* \rb of Shecaniah|לִשְׁכַנְיָ֣ה\rb* \rb son|בֶן־\rb* \rb of Arah,|אָרַ֑ח\rb* \rb and his son|בְּנ֔וֹ\rb* \rb Jehohanan|וִֽיהוֹחָנָ֣ן\rb* \rb had married|לָקַ֕ח\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the daughter|בַּת־\rb* \rb of Meshullam|מְשֻׁלָּ֖ם\rb* \rb son|בֶּ֥ן\rb* \rb of Berechiah.|בֶּֽרֶכְיָֽה׃\rb*
\p \v 19 \rb Moreover,|גַּ֣ם\rb* \rb these nobles kept|הָי֤וּ\rb* \rb reporting|אֹמְרִים֙\rb* \rb to me|לְפָנַ֔י\rb* \rb Tobiah’s good deeds,|טוֹבֹתָ֗יו\rb* \rb and they relayed|מוֹצִיאִ֖ים\rb* \rb my words|וּדְבָרַ֕י\rb* \rb to him.|ל֑וֹ\rb*\rb |הָי֥וּ\rb* \rb And Tobiah|טוֹבִיָּ֖ה\rb* \rb sent|שָׁלַ֥ח\rb* \rb letters|אִגְּר֛וֹת\rb* \rb to intimidate me.|לְיָֽרְאֵֽנִי׃\rb*
\c 7
\s1 Securing the City
\p \v 1 \rb |וַיְהִ֗י\rb* \rb When|כַּאֲשֶׁ֤ר\rb* \rb the wall|הַחוֹמָ֔ה\rb* \rb had been rebuilt|נִבְנְתָה֙\rb* \rb and I had set the doors|הַדְּלָת֑וֹת\rb* \rb in place,|וָאַעֲמִ֖יד\rb* \rb the gatekeepers,|הַשּׁוֹעֲרִ֥ים\rb* \rb singers,|וְהַמְשֹׁרְרִ֖ים\rb* \rb and Levites|וְהַלְוִיִּֽם׃\rb* \rb were appointed.|וַיִּפָּֽקְד֛וּ\rb*
\p \v 2 \rb Then I put my brother|אָחִ֗י\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb Hanani|חֲנָ֣נִי\rb* \rb in charge|וָאֲצַוֶּ֞ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb of|עַל־\rb* \rb Jerusalem,|יְרוּשָׁלִָ֑ם\rb* \rb along with Hananiah|חֲנַנְיָ֛ה\rb* \rb the commander|שַׂ֥ר\rb* \rb of the fortress,|הַבִּירָ֖ה\rb* \rb because|כִּי־\rb* \rb he|הוּא֙\rb* \rb was a faithful|אֱמֶ֔ת\rb* \rb man|כְּאִ֣ישׁ\rb* \rb who feared|וְיָרֵ֥א\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb God|הָאֱלֹהִ֖ים\rb* \rb more than most.|מֵרַבִּֽים׃\rb* \v 3 \rb And I told|וַיֹּאמֶר\rb* \rb them,|לָהֶ֗ם\rb* \rb “Do not|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb open|יִפָּֽתְח֞וּ\rb* \rb the gates|שַׁעֲרֵ֤י\rb* \rb of Jerusalem|יְרוּשָׁלִַ֙ם֙\rb* \rb until|עַד־\rb* \rb the sun|הַשֶּׁ֔מֶשׁ\rb* \rb is hot.|חֹ֣ם\rb* \rb While|וְעַ֨ד\rb* \rb the guards|הֵ֥ם\rb* \rb are on duty,|עֹמְדִ֛ים\rb* \rb keep the doors|הַדְּלָת֖וֹת\rb* \rb shut|יָגִ֥יפוּ\rb* \rb and securely fastened.|וֶאֱחֹ֑זוּ\rb* \rb And appoint|וְהַעֲמֵ֗יד\rb* \rb the residents|יֹשְׁבֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Jerusalem|יְרוּשָׁלִַ֔ם\rb* \rb as guards,|מִשְׁמְרוֹת֙\rb* \rb some|אִ֚ישׁ\rb* \rb at their posts|בְּמִשְׁמָר֔וֹ\rb* \rb and some|וְאִ֖ישׁ\rb* \rb at|נֶ֥גֶד\rb* \rb their own homes.”|בֵּיתֽוֹ׃\rb*
\s1 The List of Returning Exiles
\r \ref Ezra 2:1–67|EZR 2:1-67\ref*)
\p \v 4 \rb Now the city|וְהָעִ֞יר\rb* \rb was large|וּגְדוֹלָ֔ה\rb* \rb and spacious,|רַחֲבַ֤ת\rb*\rb |יָדַ֙יִם֙\rb* \rb but there were few|מְעַ֖ט\rb* \rb people|וְהָעָ֥ם\rb* \rb in it,|בְּתוֹכָ֑הּ\rb* \rb and the houses|בָּתִּ֖ים\rb* \rb had not yet|וְאֵ֥ין\rb* \rb been rebuilt.|בְּנוּיִֽם׃\rb* \v 5 \rb Then my God|אֱלֹהַי֙\rb* \rb put it|וַיִּתֵּ֤ן\rb* \rb into|אֶל־\rb* \rb my heart|לִבִּ֔י\rb* \rb to assemble|וָאֶקְבְּצָ֞ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the nobles,|הַחֹרִ֧ים\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb the officials,|הַסְּגָנִ֛ים\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and the people|הָעָ֖ם\rb* \rb to be enrolled by genealogy.|לְהִתְיַחֵ֑שׂ\rb* \rb I found|וָֽאֶמְצָ֗א\rb* \rb the genealogical|הַיַּ֙חַשׂ֙\rb* \rb register|סֵ֤פֶר\rb* \rb of those who had first returned,|הָעוֹלִ֣ים\rb*\rb |בָּרִאשׁוֹנָ֔ה\rb* \rb and I found|וָאֶמְצָ֖א\rb* \rb the following written|כָּת֥וּב\rb* \rb in it:|בּֽוֹ׃פ\rb*
\p \v 6 \rb These|אֵ֣לֶּה׀\rb* \rb are the people|בְּנֵ֣י\rb* \rb of the province|הַמְּדִינָ֗ה\rb* \rb who came up|הָעֹלִים֙\rb* \rb from the captivity|מִשְּׁבִ֣י\rb* \rb of the exiles|הַגּוֹלָ֔ה\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb carried away|הֶגְלָ֔ה\rb* \rb to Babylon|בָּבֶ֑ל\rb* \rb by Nebuchadnezzar|נְבוּכַדְנֶצַּ֖ר\rb* \rb its king.|מֶ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb They returned|וַיָּשׁ֧וּבוּ\rb* \rb to Jerusalem|לִֽירוּשָׁלִַ֛ם\rb* \rb and Judah,|וְלִיהוּדָ֖ה\rb* \rb each|אִ֥ישׁ\rb* \rb to his own town,|לְעִירֽוֹ׃\rb* \v 7 \rb accompanied|הַבָּאִ֣ים\rb* \rb by|עִם־\rb* \rb Zerubbabel,|זְרֻבָּבֶ֗ל\rb* \rb Jeshua,|יֵשׁ֡וּעַ\rb* \rb Nehemiah,|נְחֶמְיָ֡ה\rb* \rb Azariah,|עֲ֠זַרְיָה\rb* \rb Raamiah,|רַֽעַמְיָ֨ה\rb* \rb Nahamani,|נַחֲמָ֜נִי\rb* \rb Mordecai,|מָרְדֳּכַ֥י\rb* \rb Bilshan,|בִּלְשָׁ֛ן\rb* \rb Mispereth,|מִסְפֶּ֥רֶת\rb* \rb Bigvai,|בִּגְוַ֖י\rb* \rb Nehum,|נְח֣וּם\rb* \rb and Baanah.|בַּעֲנָ֑ה\rb*\f + \fr 7:7 \ft Parallel text at \ref Ezra 2:2|EZR 2:2\ref* \fqa accompanied by Zerubbabel, Jeshua, Nehemiah, Seraiah, Reelaiah, Mordecai, Bilshan, Mispar, Bigvai, Rehum, and Baanah\f*
\p \rb This is the count|מִסְפַּ֕ר\rb* \rb of the men|אַנְשֵׁ֖י\rb*\rb |עַ֥ם\rb* \rb of Israel:|יִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃ס\rb*
