\li1 \v 64 \rb These men|אֵ֗לֶּה\rb* \rb searched for|בִּקְשׁ֧וּ\rb* \rb their family records,|כְתָבָ֛ם\rb*\rb |הַמִּתְיַחְשִׂ֖ים\rb* \rb but they could not|וְלֹ֣א\rb* \rb find them|נִמְצָ֑א\rb* \rb and so were excluded|וַיְגֹֽאֲל֖וּ\rb* \rb from|מִן־\rb* \rb the priesthood as unclean.|הַכְּהֻנָּֽה׃\rb* \v 65 \rb The governor|הַתִּרְשָׁ֙תָא֙\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb ordered|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb* \rb them|לָהֶ֔ם\rb* \rb not|לֹא־\rb* \rb to eat|יֹאכְל֖וּ\rb* \rb the most holy things|מִקֹּ֣דֶשׁ\rb*\rb |הַקֳּדָשִׁ֑ים\rb* \rb until|עַ֛ד\rb* \rb there was|עֲמֹ֥ד\rb* \rb a priest|הַכֹּהֵ֖ן\rb* \rb to consult the Urim|לְאוּרִ֥ים\rb* \rb and Thummim.|וְתוּמִּֽים׃\rb*\f + \fr 7:65 \ft Literally \fqa Lights and Perfections\f*
\p \v 66 \rb The whole|כָּל־\rb* \rb assembly|הַקָּהָ֖ל\rb* \rb numbered|כְּאֶחָ֑ד\rb* \rb 42,360,|אַרְבַּ֣ע\rb*\rb |רִבּ֔וֹא\rb*\rb |אַלְפַּ֖יִם\rb*\rb |שְׁלֹשׁ־\rb*\rb |מֵא֥וֹת\rb*\rb |וְשִׁשִּֽׁים׃\rb* \v 67 \rb in addition to|מִ֠לְּבַד\rb* \rb their|וְלָהֶ֗ם\rb* \rb 7,337|שִׁבְעַ֣ת\rb*\rb |אֲלָפִ֔ים\rb*\rb |שְׁלֹ֥שׁ\rb*\rb |מֵא֖וֹת\rb*\rb |שְׁלֹשִׁ֣ים\rb*\rb |וְשִׁבְעָ֑ה\rb* \rb menservants|עַבְדֵיהֶ֤ם\rb* \rb and maidservants,|וְאַמְהֹֽתֵיהֶם֙\rb*\rb |אֵ֔לֶּה\rb* \rb as well as their 245|מָאתַ֖יִם\rb*\rb |וְאַרְבָּעִ֥ים\rb*\rb |וַחֲמִשָּֽׁה׃ס\rb* \rb male and female singers.|מְשֹֽׁרֲרִים֙\rb*\rb |וּמְשֹׁ֣רֲר֔וֹת\rb* \v 68 \rb They had 736 horses, 245 mules,|\rb*\f + \fr 7:68 \ft Some Hebrew manuscripts (see also \ref Ezra 2:66|EZR 2:66\ref*); most Hebrew manuscripts do not include this verse.\f* \v 69 \rb 435|אַרְבַּ֥ע\rb*\rb |מֵא֖וֹת\rb*\rb |שְׁלֹשִׁ֣ים\rb*\rb |וַחֲמִשָּׁ֑הס\rb* \rb camels,|גְּמַלִּ֕ים\rb* \rb and 6,720|שֵׁ֣שֶׁת\rb*\rb |אֲלָפִ֔ים\rb*\rb |שְׁבַ֥ע\rb*\rb |מֵא֖וֹת\rb*\rb |וְעֶשְׂרִֽים׃\rb* \rb donkeys.|חֲמֹרִ֕ים\rb*
\s1 Offerings by the Exiles
