\s1 Ezra Reads the Law
\r \ref Deuteronomy 31:9–13|DEU 31:9-13\ref*)
\p \v 1 \rb At that time all|כָל־\rb* \rb the people|הָעָם֙\rb* \rb gathered|וַיֵּאָסְפ֤וּ\rb* \rb together|כְּאִ֣ישׁ\rb*\rb |אֶחָ֔ד\rb* \rb in|אֶל־\rb* \rb the square|הָ֣רְח֔וֹב\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֖ר\rb* \rb before|לִפְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb the Water|הַמָּ֑יִם\rb* \rb Gate,|שַֽׁעַר־\rb* \rb and they asked|וַיֹּֽאמְרוּ֙\rb* \rb Ezra|לְעֶזְרָ֣א\rb* \rb the scribe|הַסֹּפֵ֔ר\rb* \rb to bring out|לְהָבִ֗יא\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the Book|סֵ֙פֶר֙\rb* \rb of the Law|תּוֹרַ֣ת\rb* \rb of Moses,|מֹשֶׁ֔ה\rb* \rb which|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb had commanded|צִוָּ֥ה\rb* \rb for|אֶת־\rb* \rb Israel.|יִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃\rb*
\p \v 2 \rb On the first|אֶחָ֖ד\rb* \rb day|בְּי֥וֹם\rb* \rb of the seventh|הַשְּׁבִיעִֽי׃\rb* \rb month,|לַחֹ֥דֶשׁ\rb* \rb Ezra|עֶזְרָ֣א\rb* \rb the priest|הַ֠כֹּהֵן\rb*\rb |אֶֽת־\rb* \rb brought|וַיָּבִ֣יא\rb* \rb the Law|הַתּוֹרָ֞ה\rb* \rb before|לִפְנֵ֤י\rb* \rb the assembly|הַקָּהָל֙\rb* \rb of men|מֵאִ֣ישׁ\rb* \rb and|וְעַד־\rb* \rb women|אִשָּׁ֔ה\rb* \rb and all|וְכֹ֖ל\rb* \rb who could listen|לִשְׁמֹ֑עַ\rb* \rb and understand.|מֵבִ֣ין\rb* \v 3 \rb So Ezra read|וַיִּקְרָא־\rb* \rb it aloud|בוֹ֩\rb* \rb from|מִן־\rb* \rb daybreak|הָאוֹר֙\rb* \rb until|עַד־\rb* \rb noon|מַחֲצִ֣ית\rb*\rb |הַיּ֔וֹם\rb* \rb as he faced|לִפְנֵ֨י\rb* \rb the square|הָרְח֜וֹב\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר׀\rb* \rb before|לִפְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb the Water|הַמַּ֗יִם\rb* \rb Gate,|שַֽׁעַר־\rb* \rb in front of|נֶ֛גֶד\rb* \rb the men|הָאֲנָשִׁ֥ים\rb* \rb and women|וְהַנָּשִׁ֖ים\rb* \rb and those who could understand.|וְהַמְּבִינִ֑ים\rb*
\p \rb And all|כָל־\rb* \rb the people|הָעָ֖ם\rb* \rb listened attentively to|וְאָזְנֵ֥י\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb the Book|סֵ֥פֶר\rb* \rb of the Law.|הַתּוֹרָֽה׃\rb*
\p \v 4 \rb Ezra|עֶזְרָ֣א\rb* \rb the scribe|הַסֹּפֵ֗ר\rb* \rb stood|וַֽיַּעֲמֹ֞ד\rb* \rb on|עַֽל־\rb* \rb a high wooden|עֵץ֮\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb platform|מִגְדַּל־\rb* \rb built|עָשׂ֣וּ\rb* \rb for this occasion.|לַדָּבָר֒\rb* \rb At his|עַל־\rb* \rb right side|יְמִינ֑וֹ\rb* \rb stood|וַיַּֽעֲמֹ֣ד\rb* \rb Mattithiah,|מַתִּתְיָ֡ה\rb* \rb Shema,|וְשֶׁ֡מַע\rb* \rb Anaiah,|וַ֠עֲנָיָה\rb* \rb Uriah,|וְאוּרִיָּ֧ה\rb* \rb Hilkiah,|וְחִלְקִיָּ֛ה\rb* \rb and Maaseiah,|וּמַעֲשֵׂיָ֖ה\rb* \rb and at his left|וּמִשְּׂמֹאל֗וֹ\rb* \rb were Pedaiah,|פְּ֠דָיָה\rb* \rb Mishael,|וּמִֽישָׁאֵ֧ל\rb* \rb Malchijah,|וּמַלְכִּיָּ֛ה\rb* \rb Hashum,|וְחָשֻׁ֥ם\rb* \rb Hash-baddanah,|וְחַשְׁבַּדָּ֖נָה\rb* \rb Zechariah,|זְכַרְיָ֥ה\rb* \rb and Meshullam.|מְשֻׁלָּֽם׃פ\rb*
\p \v 5 \rb Ezra|עֶזְרָ֤א\rb* \rb opened|וַיִּפְתַּ֨ח\rb* \rb the book|הַסֵּ֙פֶר֙\rb* \rb in full view|לְעֵינֵ֣י\rb* \rb of all|כָל־\rb* \rb the people,|הָעָ֔ם\rb* \rb since|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb he was|הָיָ֑ה\rb* \rb standing above them|מֵעַ֥ל\rb* \rb all,|כָּל־\rb*\rb |הָעָ֖ם\rb* \rb and as he opened it,|וּכְפִתְח֖וֹ\rb* \rb all|כָל־\rb* \rb the people|הָעָֽם׃\rb* \rb stood up.|עָֽמְד֥וּ\rb* \v 6 \rb Then Ezra|עֶזְרָ֔א\rb* \rb blessed|וַיְבָ֣רֶךְ\rb* \rb the LORD,|יְהוָ֥ה\rb* \rb the great|הַגָּד֑וֹל\rb* \rb God,|הָאֱלֹהִ֖ים\rb* \rb and with their hands|יְדֵיהֶ֔ם\rb* \rb uplifted,|בְּמֹ֣עַל\rb* \rb all|כָל־\rb* \rb the people|הָעָ֜ם\rb* \rb said,|וַיַּֽעֲנ֨וּ\rb* \rb “Amen,|אָמֵ֤ן׀\rb* \rb Amen!”|אָמֵן֙\rb* \rb Then they bowed down|וַיִּקְּד֧וּ\rb* \rb and worshiped|וַיִּשְׁתַּחֲוֻּ֛\rb* \rb the LORD|לַיהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb with their faces|אַפַּ֥יִם\rb* \rb to the ground.|אָֽרְצָה׃\rb*
\p \v 7 \rb The Levites—|וְהַלְוִיִּ֔ם\rb*  \rb Jeshua,|וְיֵשׁ֡וּעַ\rb* \rb Bani,|וּבָנִ֡י\rb* \rb Sherebiah,|וְשֵׁרֵ֥בְיָ֣ה׀\rb* \rb Jamin,|יָמִ֡ין\rb* \rb Akkub,|עַקּ֡וּב\rb* \rb Shabbethai,|שַׁבְּתַ֣י׀\rb* \rb Hodiah,|הֽוֹדִיָּ֡ה\rb* \rb Maaseiah,|מַעֲשֵׂיָ֡ה\rb* \rb Kelita,|קְלִיטָ֣א\rb* \rb Azariah,|עֲזַרְיָה֩\rb* \rb Jozabad,|יוֹזָבָ֨ד\rb* \rb Hanan,|חָנָ֤ן\rb* \rb and Pelaiah—|פְּלָאיָה֙\rb*  \rb instructed|מְבִינִ֥ים\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the people|הָעָ֖ם\rb* \rb in the Law|לַתּוֹרָ֑ה\rb* \rb as they|וְהָעָ֖ם\rb* \rb stood in|עַל־\rb* \rb their places.|עָמְדָֽם׃\rb* \v 8 \rb So they read|וַֽיִּקְרְא֥וּ\rb* \rb from the Book|בַסֵּ֛פֶר\rb* \rb of the Law|בְּתוֹרַ֥ת\rb* \rb of God,|הָאֱלֹהִ֖ים\rb* \rb explaining it|מְפֹרָ֑שׁ\rb*\f + \fr 8:8 \ft Or \fqa translating it \ft or \fqa paragraph by paragraph\f* \rb and giving|וְשׂ֣וֹם\rb* \rb insight,|שֶׂ֔כֶל\rb* \rb so that the people could understand|וַיָּבִ֖ינוּ\rb* \rb what was being read.|בַּמִּקְרָֽא׃ס\rb*
\p \v 9 \rb Nehemiah|נְחֶמְיָ֣ה\rb* \rb the governor,|הַתִּרְשָׁ֡תָא\rb* \rb Ezra|וְעֶזְרָ֣א\rb* \rb the priest|הַכֹּהֵ֣ן׀\rb* \rb and scribe,|הַסֹּפֵ֡ר\rb* \rb and the Levites|וְהַלְוִיִּם֩\rb* \rb who were instructing|הַמְּבִינִ֨ים\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the people|הָעָ֜ם\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb* \rb to all|לְכָל־\rb* \rb of them,|הָעָ֗ם\rb* \rb “This|הוּא֙\rb* \rb day|הַיּ֤וֹם\rb* \rb is holy|קָדֹֽשׁ־\rb* \rb to the LORD|לַיהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb your God.|אֱלֹהֵיכֶ֔ם\rb* \rb Do not|אַל־\rb* \rb mourn|תִּֽתְאַבְּל֖וּ\rb*\rb |וְאַל־\rb* \rb or weep.”|תִּבְכּ֑וּ\rb*
\p \rb For|כִּ֤י\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the people|הָעָ֔ם\rb* \rb were weeping|בוֹכִים֙\rb* \rb as they heard|כְּשָׁמְעָ֖ם\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the words|דִּבְרֵ֥י\rb* \rb of the Law.|הַתּוֹרָֽה׃\rb*
\p \v 10 \rb Then Nehemiah told|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb* \rb them,|לָהֶ֡ם\rb* \rb “Go|לְכוּ֩\rb* \rb and eat|אִכְל֨וּ\rb* \rb what is rich,|מַשְׁמַנִּ֜ים\rb* \rb drink|וּשְׁת֣וּ\rb* \rb what is sweet,|מַֽמְתַקִּ֗ים\rb* \rb and send out|וְשִׁלְח֤וּ\rb* \rb portions|מָנוֹת֙\rb* \rb to those who have nothing|לְאֵ֣ין\rb* \rb prepared,|נָכ֣וֹן\rb* \rb since|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb today|הַיּ֖וֹם\rb* \rb is holy|קָד֥וֹשׁ\rb* \rb to our Lord.|לַאֲדֹנֵ֑ינוּ\rb* \rb Do not|וְאַל־\rb* \rb grieve,|תֵּ֣עָצֵ֔בוּ\rb* \rb for|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb the joy|חֶדְוַ֥ת\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb is|הִ֥יא\rb* \rb your strength.”|מָֽעֻזְּכֶֽם׃\rb*
\p \v 11 \rb And the Levites|וְהַלְוִיִּ֞ם\rb* \rb calmed|מַחְשִׁ֤ים\rb* \rb all|לְכָל־\rb* \rb the people,|הָעָם֙\rb* \rb saying,|לֵאמֹ֣ר\rb* \rb “Be still,|הַ֔סּוּ\rb* \rb since|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb today|הַיּ֖וֹם\rb* \rb is holy.|קָדֹ֑שׁ\rb* \rb Do not|וְאַל־\rb* \rb grieve.”|תֵּעָצֵֽבוּ׃\rb*
\p \v 12 \rb |וַיֵּלְכ֨וּ\rb* \rb Then all|כָל־\rb* \rb the people|הָעָ֜ם\rb* \rb began to eat|לֶאֱכֹ֤ל\rb* \rb and drink,|וְלִשְׁתּוֹת֙\rb* \rb to send out|וּלְשַׁלַּ֣ח\rb* \rb portions,|מָנ֔וֹת\rb* \rb and|וְלַעֲשׂ֖וֹת\rb* \rb to rejoice|שִׂמְחָ֣ה\rb* \rb greatly,|גְדוֹלָ֑ה\rb* \rb because|כִּ֤י\rb* \rb they understood|הֵבִ֙ינוּ֙\rb* \rb the words|בַּדְּבָרִ֔ים\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb had been made known|הוֹדִ֖יעוּ\rb* \rb to them.|לָהֶֽם׃ס\rb*
\s1 The Feast of Tabernacles
\r \ref Leviticus 23:33–44|LEV 23:33-44\ref*; \ref Zechariah 14:16–21|ZEC 14:16-21\ref*)
\p \v 13 \rb On the second|הַשֵּׁנִ֡י\rb* \rb day of the month,|וּבַיּ֣וֹם\rb* \rb the heads|רָאשֵׁ֨י\rb* \rb of all|לְכָל־\rb* \rb the families,|הָאָב֜וֹת\rb*\rb |הָעָ֗ם\rb* \rb along with the priests|הַכֹּֽהֲנִים֙\rb* \rb and Levites,|וְהַלְוִיִּ֔ם\rb* \rb gathered|נֶאֶסְפוּ֩\rb* \rb around|אֶל־\rb* \rb Ezra|עֶזְרָ֖א\rb* \rb the scribe|הַסֹּפֵ֑ר\rb* \rb to study|וּלְהַשְׂכִּ֖יל\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb the words|דִּבְרֵ֥י\rb* \rb of the Law.|הַתּוֹרָֽה׃\rb* \v 14 \rb And they found|וַֽיִּמְצְא֖וּ\rb* \rb written|כָּת֣וּב\rb* \rb in the Law,|בַּתּוֹרָ֑ה\rb* \rb which|אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb had commanded|צִוָּ֤ה\rb* \rb through|בְּיַד־\rb* \rb Moses,|מֹשֶׁ֔ה\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁר֩\rb* \rb the Israelites|בְנֵֽי־\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵ֧ל\rb* \rb were to dwell|יֵשְׁב֨וּ\rb* \rb in booths|בַּסֻּכּ֛וֹת\rb*\f + \fr 8:14 \ft Or \fqa tabernacles \ft or \fqa shelters\ft ; also in verses 15, 16, and 17\f* \rb during the feast|בֶּחָ֖ג\rb* \rb of the seventh|הַשְּׁבִיעִֽי׃\rb* \rb month,|בַּחֹ֥דֶשׁ\rb* \v 15 \rb and that|וַאֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb they should proclaim|יַשְׁמִ֗יעוּ\rb* \rb this message|ק֥וֹל\rb* \rb and spread it|וְיַעֲבִ֨ירוּ\rb* \rb throughout|בְּכָל־\rb* \rb their towns|עָרֵיהֶם֮\rb* \rb and in Jerusalem,|וּבִירוּשָׁלִַ֣ם\rb* \rb saying,|לֵאמֹר֒\rb* \rb “Go out|צְא֣וּ\rb* \rb to the hill country|הָהָ֗ר\rb* \rb and bring back|וְהָבִ֙יאוּ֙\rb* \rb branches|עֲלֵי־\rb* \rb of olive,|זַ֙יִת֙\rb*\rb |וַעֲלֵי־\rb* \rb wild olive,|שֶׁ֔מֶן\rb*\f + \fr 8:15 \ft Or \fqa pine\ft ; literally \fqa oil tree\f*\rb |וַעֲלֵ֤י\rb* \rb myrtle,|הֲדַס֙\rb*\rb |וַעֲלֵ֣י\rb* \rb palm,|תְמָרִ֔ים\rb*\rb |וַעֲלֵ֖י\rb* \rb and other leafy|עָבֹ֑ת\rb* \rb trees,|עֵ֣ץ\rb* \rb to make|לַעֲשֹׂ֥ת\rb* \rb booths,|סֻכֹּ֖ת\rb* \rb as it is written.”|כַּכָּתֽוּב׃פ\rb*\f + \fr 8:15 \ft See \ref Leviticus 23:37–40|LEV 23:37-40\ref*.\f*
\p \v 16 \rb And the people|הָעָם֮\rb* \rb went out,|וַיֵּצְא֣וּ\rb* \rb brought back branches,|וַיָּבִיאוּ֒\rb* \rb and made|וַיַּעֲשׂוּ֩\rb*\rb |לָהֶ֨ם\rb* \rb booths|סֻכּ֜וֹת\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb their own|אִ֤ישׁ\rb* \rb rooftops,|גַּגּוֹ֙\rb* \rb in their courtyards,|וּבְחַצְרֹ֣תֵיהֶ֔ם\rb* \rb in the courts|וּבְחַצְר֖וֹת\rb* \rb of the house|בֵּ֣ית\rb* \rb of God,|הָאֱלֹהִ֑ים\rb* \rb and in the squares|וּבִרְחוֹב֙\rb* \rb by the Water|הַמַּ֔יִם\rb* \rb Gate|שַׁ֣עַר\rb* \rb and|וּבִרְח֖וֹב\rb* \rb by the Gate|שַׁ֥עַר\rb* \rb of Ephraim.|אֶפְרָֽיִם׃\rb* \v 17 \rb The whole|כָֽל־\rb* \rb assembly|הַ֠קָּהָל\rb* \rb that had returned|הַשָּׁבִ֨ים\rb* \rb from|מִן־\rb* \rb exile|הַשְּׁבִ֥י׀\rb* \rb made|וַיַּֽעֲשׂ֣וּ\rb* \rb booths|סֻכּוֹת֮\rb* \rb and lived|וַיֵּשְׁב֣וּ\rb* \rb in them.|בַסֻּכּוֹת֒\rb*\rb |כִּ֣י\rb* \rb From the days|מִימֵי֩\rb* \rb of Joshua|יֵשׁ֨וּעַ\rb*\f + \fr 8:17 \ft Hebrew \fqa Jeshua\ft , a variant of \fqa Joshua\f* \rb son|בִּן־\rb* \rb of Nun|נ֥וּן\rb* \rb until|עַ֖ד\rb* \rb that|הַה֑וּא\rb* \rb day,|הַיּ֣וֹם\rb* \rb the Israelites|בְּנֵ֣י\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb* \rb had not|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb celebrated|עָשׂ֡וּ\rb* \rb like this.|כֵּן֙\rb* \rb And there was|וַתְּהִ֥י\rb* \rb great|גְּדוֹלָ֥ה\rb* \rb rejoicing.|שִׂמְחָ֖ה\rb*
\p \v 18 \rb Day|י֣וֹם׀\rb* \rb after day,|בְּי֔וֹם\rb* \rb from|מִן־\rb* \rb the first|הָֽרִאשׁ֔וֹן\rb* \rb day|הַיּוֹם֙\rb* \rb to|עַ֖ד\rb* \rb the last,|הָאַחֲר֑וֹן\rb* \rb Ezra read|וַ֠יִּקְרָא\rb* \rb from the Book|בְּסֵ֨פֶר\rb* \rb of the Law|תּוֹרַ֤ת\rb* \rb of God.|הָאֱלֹהִים֙\rb* \rb The Israelites kept|וַיַּֽעֲשׂוּ־\rb* \rb the feast|חָג֙\rb* \rb for seven|שִׁבְעַ֣ת\rb* \rb days,|הַיּ֣וֹם\rb* \rb and on the eighth|הַשְּׁמִינִ֛י\rb* \rb day|יָמִ֔ים\rb*\rb |וּבַיּ֧וֹם\rb* \rb they held an assembly,|עֲצֶ֖רֶת\rb* \rb according to the ordinance.|כַּמִּשְׁפָּֽט׃פ\rb*
\c 9
\s1 The People Confess Their Sins
\p \v 1 \rb On the twenty-fourth|עֶשְׂרִ֨ים\rb*\rb |וְאַרְבָּעָ֜ה\rb* \rb day|וּבְיוֹם֩\rb* \rb of the same|הַזֶּ֗ה\rb* \rb month,|לַחֹ֣דֶשׁ\rb* \rb the Israelites|בְנֵֽי־\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵל֙\rb* \rb gathered together,|נֶאֶסְפ֤וּ\rb* \rb fasting|בְּצ֣וֹם\rb* \rb and wearing sackcloth,|וּבְשַׂקִּ֔ים\rb* \rb with dust|וַאֲדָמָ֖ה\rb* \rb on their heads.|עֲלֵיהֶֽם׃\rb* \v 2 \rb Those of Israelite|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb* \rb descent|זֶ֣רַע\rb* \rb separated themselves|וַיִּבָּֽדְלוּ֙\rb* \rb from all|מִכֹּ֖ל\rb* \rb the foreigners,|בְּנֵ֣י\rb*\rb |נֵכָ֑ר\rb* \rb and they stood|וַיַּעַמְד֗וּ\rb* \rb and confessed|וַיִּתְוַדּוּ֙\rb*\rb |עַל־\rb* \rb their sins|חַטֹּ֣אתֵיהֶ֔ם\rb* \rb and the iniquities|וַעֲוֺנ֖וֹת\rb* \rb of their fathers.|אֲבֹתֵיהֶֽם׃\rb*
\p \v 3 \rb While they stood|וַיָּק֙וּמוּ֙\rb* \rb in|עַל־\rb* \rb their places,|עָמְדָ֔ם\rb* \rb they read|וַֽיִּקְרְא֗וּ\rb* \rb from the Book|בְּסֵ֨פֶר\rb* \rb of the Law|תּוֹרַ֧ת\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֛ה\rb* \rb their God|אֱלֹהֵיהֶ֖ם\rb* \rb for a quarter|רְבִעִ֣ית\rb* \rb of the day,|הַיּ֑וֹם\rb* \rb and they spent another quarter of the day|וּרְבִעִית֙\rb* \rb in confession|מִתְוַדִּ֣ים\rb* \rb and worship|וּמִֽשְׁתַּחֲוִ֔ים\rb* \rb of the LORD|לַיהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb their God.|אֱלֹהֵיהֶֽם׃פ\rb*
\p \v 4 \rb And the Levites—|הַלְוִיִּ֗ם\rb*  \rb Jeshua,|יֵשׁ֨וּעַ\rb* \rb Bani,|וּבָנִ֜י\rb* \rb Kadmiel,|קַדְמִיאֵ֧ל\rb* \rb Shebaniah,|שְׁבַנְיָ֛ה\rb* \rb Bunni,|בֻּנִּ֥י\rb* \rb Sherebiah,|שֵׁרֵבְיָ֖ה\rb* \rb Bani,|בָּנִ֣י\rb* \rb and Chenani—|כְנָ֑נִי\rb*  \rb stood|וַיָּ֜קָם\rb* \rb on|עַֽל־\rb* \rb the raised platform|מַֽעֲלֵ֣ה\rb* \rb and cried out|וַֽיִּזְעֲקוּ֙\rb* \rb in a loud|גָּד֔וֹל\rb* \rb voice|בְּק֣וֹל\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb their God.|אֱלֹהֵיהֶֽם׃\rb* \v 5 \rb Then the Levites—|הַלְוִיִּ֡ם\rb* \rb Jeshua,|יֵשׁ֣וּעַ\rb* \rb Kadmiel,|וְ֠קַדְמִיאֵל\rb* \rb Bani,|בָּנִ֨י\rb* \rb Hashabneiah,|חֲשַׁבְנְיָ֜ה\rb* \rb Sherebiah,|שֵׁרֵֽבְיָ֤ה\rb* \rb Hodiah,|הֽוֹדִיָּה֙\rb* \rb Shebaniah,|שְׁבַנְיָ֣ה\rb* \rb and Pethahiah—|פְתַֽחְיָ֔ה\rb* \rb said,|וַיֹּאמְר֣וּ\rb* \rb “Stand up|ק֗וּמוּ\rb* \rb and bless|בָּרֲכוּ֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹֽהֵיכֶ֔ם\rb* \rb from|מִן־\rb* \rb everlasting|הָעוֹלָ֖ם\rb* \rb to|עַד־\rb* \rb everlasting:|הָעוֹלָ֑ם\rb*
\b 
\q1 \rb Blessed be|וִיבָֽרְכוּ֙\rb* \rb Your glorious|כְּבוֹדֶ֔ךָ\rb* \rb name,|שֵׁ֣ם\rb*
\q2 \rb and may it be exalted|וּמְרוֹמַ֥ם\rb*
\q2 \rb above|עַל־\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb blessing|בְּרָכָ֖ה\rb* \rb and praise.|וּתְהִלָּֽה׃\rb*
\q1 \v 6 \rb You|אַתָּה־\rb*\rb |ה֣וּא\rb* \rb alone|לְבַדֶּךָ֒\rb*\rb |אַתְּ\rb* \rb are the LORD.|יְהוָה֮\rb*
\q2 \rb You created|עָשִׂ֡יתָ\rb*\rb |אֶֽת־\rb* \rb the heavens,|הַשָּׁמַיִם֩\rb*
\q1 \rb the highest heavens|שְׁמֵ֨י\rb*\rb |הַשָּׁמַ֜יִם\rb* \rb with all|וְכָל־\rb* \rb their host,|צְבָאָ֗ם\rb*
\q2 \rb the earth|הָאָ֜רֶץ\rb* \rb and all|וְכָל־\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֤ר\rb* \rb is on it,|עָלֶ֙יהָ֙\rb*
\q2 \rb the seas|הַיַּמִּים֙\rb* \rb and all|וְכָל־\rb* \rb that is|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb in them.|בָּהֶ֔ם\rb*
\q1 \rb You|וְאַתָּ֖ה\rb* \rb give life|מְחַיֶּ֣ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb to all things,|כֻּלָּ֑ם\rb*
\q2 \rb and the host|וּצְבָ֥א\rb* \rb of heaven|הַשָּׁמַ֖יִם\rb* \rb worships|מִשְׁתַּחֲוִֽים׃\rb* \rb You.|לְךָ֥\rb*
\b 
\q1 \v 7 \rb You|אַתָּה־\rb*\rb |הוּא֙\rb* \rb are the LORD,|יְהוָ֣ה\rb*
\q2 \rb the God|הָאֱלֹהִ֔ים\rb* \rb who|אֲשֶׁ֤ר\rb* \rb chose|בָּחַ֙רְתָּ֙\rb* \rb Abram,|בְּאַבְרָ֔ם\rb*
\q1 \rb who brought him|וְהוֹצֵאת֖וֹ\rb* \rb out of Ur|מֵא֣וּר\rb* \rb of the Chaldeans|כַּשְׂדִּ֑ים\rb*
\q2 \rb and gave him|וְשַׂ֥מְתָּ\rb* \rb the name|שְּׁמ֖וֹ\rb* \rb Abraham.|אַבְרָהָֽם׃\rb*
\q1 \v 8 \rb You found|וּמָצָ֣אתָ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb his heart|לְבָבוֹ֮\rb* \rb faithful|נֶאֱמָ֣ן\rb* \rb before You,|לְפָנֶיךָ֒\rb*
\q2 \rb and made|וְכָר֨וֹת\rb* \rb a covenant|הַבְּרִ֗ית\rb* \rb with him|עִמּ֜וֹ\rb*
\q1 \rb to give|לָתֵ֡ת\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the land|אֶרֶץ֩\rb* \rb of the Canaanites|הַכְּנַעֲנִ֨י\rb* \rb and Hittites,|הַחִתִּ֜י\rb*
\q2 \rb of the Amorites|הָאֱמֹרִ֧י\rb* \rb and Perizzites,|וְהַפְּרִזִּ֛י\rb*
\q2 \rb of the Jebusites|וְהַיְבוּסִ֥י\rb* \rb and Girgashites—|וְהַגִּרְגָּשִׁ֖י\rb*
\q1 \rb to give it|לָתֵ֣ת\rb* \rb to his descendants.|לְזַרְע֑וֹ\rb*
\q2 \rb You have kept|וַתָּ֙קֶם֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Your promise,|דְּבָרֶ֔יךָ\rb*
\q2 \rb because|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb You|אָֽתָּה׃\rb* \rb are righteous.|צַדִּ֖יק\rb*
\b 
\q1 \v 9 \rb You saw|וַתֵּ֛רֶא\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the affliction|עֳנִ֥י\rb* \rb of our fathers|אֲבֹתֵ֖ינוּ\rb* \rb in Egypt;|בְּמִצְרָ֑יִם\rb*
\q2 \rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb You heard|שָׁמַ֖עְתָּ\rb* \rb their cry|זַעֲקָתָ֥ם\rb* \rb at|עַל־\rb* \rb the Red|סֽוּף׃\rb* \rb Sea.|יַם־\rb*\f + \fr 9:9 \ft Or \fqa the Sea of Reeds\f*
\q1 \v 10 \rb You performed|וַ֠תִּתֵּן\rb* \rb signs|אֹתֹ֨ת\rb* \rb and wonders|וּמֹֽפְתִ֜ים\rb* \rb against Pharaoh,|בְּפַרְעֹ֤ה\rb*
\q2 \rb all|וּבְכָל־\rb* \rb his officials,|עֲבָדָיו֙\rb* \rb and all|וּבְכָל־\rb* \rb the people|עַ֣ם\rb* \rb of his land,|אַרְצ֔וֹ\rb*
\q1 \rb for|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb You knew|יָדַ֔עְתָּ\rb*\rb |כִּ֥י\rb* \rb they had acted with arrogance|הֵזִ֖ידוּ\rb*
\q2 \rb against our fathers.|עֲלֵיהֶ֑ם\rb*
\q1 \rb You made|וַתַּֽעַשׂ־\rb* \rb a name|שֵׁ֖ם\rb* \rb for Yourself|לְךָ֥\rb*
\q2 \rb that endures to this|הַזֶּֽה׃\rb* \rb day.|כְּהַיּ֥וֹם\rb*
