\q2 \rb and Your Spirit|בְּרוּחֲךָ֛\rb* \rb admonished|וַתָּ֨עַד\rb* \rb them|בָּ֧ם\rb* \rb through|בְּיַד־\rb* \rb Your prophets.|נְבִיאֶ֖יךָ\rb*
\q1 \rb Yet they would not|וְלֹ֣א\rb* \rb listen,|הֶאֱזִ֑ינוּ\rb*
\q2 \rb so You gave them|וַֽתִּתְּנֵ֔ם\rb* \rb into the hands|בְּיַ֖ד\rb* \rb of the neighboring peoples.|עַמֵּ֥י\rb*\f + \fr 9:30 \ft Literally \fqa into the hands of the peoples of the lands\f*\rb |הָאֲרָצֹֽת׃\rb*
\q1 \v 31 \rb But in Your great|הָרַבִּ֛ים\rb* \rb compassion,|וּֽבְרַחֲמֶ֧יךָ\rb*
\q2 \rb You did not|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb put an end to them;|עֲשִׂיתָ֥ם\rb*\rb |כָּלָ֖ה\rb*
\q1 \rb nor|וְלֹ֣א\rb* \rb did You forsake them,|עֲזַבְתָּ֑ם\rb*
\q2 \rb for|כִּ֛י\rb* \rb You|אָֽתָּה׃\rb* \rb are a gracious|חַנּ֥וּן\rb* \rb and compassionate|וְרַח֖וּם\rb* \rb God.|אֵֽל־\rb*
\b 
\q1 \v 32 \rb So now,|וְעַתָּ֣ה\rb* \rb our God,|אֱ֠לֹהֵינוּ\rb* \rb the great|הַגָּד֜וֹל\rb* \rb and mighty|הַגִּבּ֣וֹר\rb* \rb and awesome|וְהַנּוֹרָא֮\rb* \rb God|הָאֵ֨ל\rb*
\q2 \rb who keeps|שׁוֹמֵ֣ר\rb* \rb His gracious|וְהַחֶסֶד֒\rb* \rb covenant,|הַבְּרִ֣ית\rb*
\q1 \rb do not|אַל־\rb* \rb view lightly|יִמְעַ֣ט\rb*\rb |לְפָנֶ֡יךָ\rb*\rb |אֵ֣ת\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the hardship|הַתְּלָאָ֣ה\rb*
\q2 \rb that|אֲֽשֶׁר־\rb* \rb has come upon us,|מְ֠צָאַתְנוּ\rb*
\q1 \rb and upon our kings|לִמְלָכֵ֨ינוּ\rb* \rb and leaders,|לְשָׂרֵ֧ינוּ\rb*
\q2 \rb our priests|וּלְכֹהֲנֵ֛ינוּ\rb* \rb and prophets,|וְלִנְבִיאֵ֥נוּ\rb*
\q1 \rb our ancestors|וְלַאֲבֹתֵ֖ינוּ\rb* \rb and all|וּלְכָל־\rb* \rb Your people,|עַמֶּ֑ךָ\rb*
\q2 \rb from the days|מִימֵי֙\rb* \rb of the kings|מַלְכֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Assyria|אַשּׁ֔וּר\rb* \rb until today.|עַ֖ד\rb*\rb |הַיּ֥וֹם\rb*\rb |הַזֶּֽה׃\rb*
\q1 \v 33 \rb You|וְאַתָּ֣ה\rb* \rb are just|צַדִּ֔יק\rb* \rb in|עַ֖ל\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb that has befallen|הַבָּ֣א\rb* \rb us,|עָלֵ֑ינוּ\rb*
\q2 \rb because|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb You have acted|עָשִׂ֖יתָ\rb* \rb faithfully,|אֱמֶ֥ת\rb*
\q2 \rb while we|וַאֲנַ֥חְנוּ\rb* \rb have acted wickedly.|הִרְשָֽׁעְנוּ׃\rb*
\q1 \v 34 \rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb Our kings|מְלָכֵ֤ינוּ\rb* \rb and leaders|שָׂרֵ֙ינוּ֙\rb* \rb and priests|כֹּהֲנֵ֣ינוּ\rb* \rb and fathers|וַאֲבֹתֵ֔ינוּ\rb*
\q2 \rb did not|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb obey|עָשׂ֖וּ\rb* \rb Your law|תּוֹרָתֶ֑ךָ\rb*\rb |וְלֹ֤א\rb*
\q1 \rb or listen|הִקְשִׁ֙יבוּ֙\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Your commandments|מִצְוֺתֶ֔יךָ\rb*
\q2 \rb and warnings|וּלְעֵ֣דְוֺתֶ֔יךָ\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb You gave|הַעִידֹ֖תָ\rb* \rb them.|בָּהֶֽם׃\rb*
\q1 \v 35 \rb For even while|וְהֵ֣ם\rb* \rb they were in their kingdom,|בְּמַלְכוּתָם֩\rb*
\q2 \rb with the abundant|הָרָ֜ב\rb* \rb goodness|וּבְטוּבְךָ֨\rb*
\q2 \rb that|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb You had given|נָתַ֣תָּ\rb* \rb them,|לָהֶ֗ם\rb*
\q1 \rb and in the spacious|הָרְחָבָ֧ה\rb* \rb and fertile|וְהַשְּׁמֵנָ֛ה\rb* \rb land|וּבְאֶ֨רֶץ\rb*
\q2 \rb that|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb You had set|נָתַ֥תָּ\rb* \rb before them,|לִפְנֵיהֶ֖ם\rb*
\q1 \rb they would not|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb serve You|עֲבָד֑וּךָ\rb*\rb |וְֽלֹא־\rb*
\q2 \rb or turn|שָׁ֔בוּ\rb* \rb from their wicked|הָרָעִֽים׃\rb* \rb ways.|מִמַּֽעַלְלֵיהֶ֖ם\rb*
\b 
\q1 \v 36 \rb So here|הִנֵּ֛ה\rb* \rb we are|אֲנַ֥חְנוּ\rb* \rb today|הַיּ֖וֹם\rb* \rb as slaves|עֲבָדִ֑ים\rb*
\q2 \rb in the land|וְהָאָ֜רֶץ\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb You gave|נָתַ֣תָּה\rb* \rb our fathers|לַאֲבֹתֵ֗ינוּ\rb* \rb to enjoy|לֶאֱכֹ֤ל\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb its fruit|פִּרְיָהּ֙\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and goodness—|טוּבָ֔הּ\rb*
\q2 \rb here|הִנֵּ֛ה\rb*\rb |עָלֶֽיהָ׃\rb* \rb we are|אֲנַ֥חְנוּ\rb* \rb as slaves!|עֲבָדִ֖ים\rb*
\q1 \v 37 \rb Its abundant|מַרְבָּ֗ה\rb* \rb harvest|וּתְבוּאָתָ֣הּ\rb* \rb goes to the kings|לַמְּלָכִ֛ים\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb*
\q2 \rb You have set|נָתַ֥תָּה\rb* \rb over us|עָלֵ֖ינוּ\rb* \rb because of our sins.|בְּחַטֹּאותֵ֑ינוּ\rb*
\q1 \rb And they rule|מֹשְׁלִ֤ים\rb* \rb over|וְעַ֣ל\rb* \rb our bodies|גְּ֠וִיֹּתֵינוּ\rb* \rb and our livestock|וּבִבְהֶמְתֵּ֙נוּ֙\rb* \rb as they please.|כִּרְצוֹנָ֔ם\rb*
\q2 \rb We|אֲנָֽחְנוּ׃פ\rb* \rb are in great|גְדוֹלָ֖ה\rb* \rb distress.|וּבְצָרָ֥ה\rb*
\p \v 38 \rb In view of all|וּבְכָל־\rb* \rb this,|זֹ֕את\rb* \rb we|אֲנַ֛חְנוּ\rb* \rb make|כֹּרְתִ֥ים\rb* \rb a binding agreement,|אֲמָנָ֖ה\rb* \rb putting it in writing|וְכֹתְבִ֑ים\rb* \rb and|וְעַל֙\rb* \rb sealing it with the names of|הֶֽחָת֔וּם\rb*\f + \fr 9:38 \ft Hebrew does not include \fqa the names of\ft .\f* \rb our leaders,|שָׂרֵ֥ינוּ\rb* \rb Levites,|לְוִיֵּ֖נוּ\rb* \rb and priests.”|כֹּהֲנֵֽינוּ׃\rb*
\c 10
\s1 Signers of the Covenant
\p \v 1 \rb Now|וְעַ֖ל\rb* \rb these were the ones who sealed the document:|הַחֲתוּמִ֑ים\rb*
\b 
\li1 \rb Nehemiah|נְחֶמְיָ֧ה\rb* \rb the governor,|הַתִּרְשָׁ֛תָא\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Hacaliah,|חֲכַלְיָ֖ה\rb*
\li1 \rb and also Zedekiah,|וְצִדְקִיָּֽה׃\rb*
\li1 \v 2 \rb Seraiah,|שְׂרָיָ֥ה\rb* \rb Azariah,|עֲזַרְיָ֖ה\rb* \rb Jeremiah,|יִרְמְיָֽה׃\rb*
\li1 \v 3 \rb Pashhur,|פַּשְׁח֥וּר\rb* \rb Amariah,|אֲמַרְיָ֖ה\rb* \rb Malchijah,|מַלְכִּיָּֽה׃\rb*
\li1 \v 4 \rb Hattush,|חַטּ֥וּשׁ\rb* \rb Shebaniah,|שְׁבַנְיָ֖ה\rb* \rb Malluch,|מַלּֽוּךְ׃\rb*
\li1 \v 5 \rb Harim,|חָרִ֥ם\rb* \rb Meremoth,|מְרֵמ֖וֹת\rb* \rb Obadiah,|עֹֽבַדְיָֽה׃\rb*
\li1 \v 6 \rb Daniel,|דָּנִיֵּ֥אל\rb* \rb Ginnethon,|גִּנְּת֖וֹן\rb* \rb Baruch,|בָּרֽוּךְ׃\rb*
\li1 \v 7 \rb Meshullam,|מְשֻׁלָּ֥ם\rb* \rb Abijah,|אֲבִיָּ֖ה\rb* \rb Mijamin,|מִיָּמִֽן׃\rb*
\li1 \v 8 \rb Maaziah,|מַֽעַזְיָ֥ה\rb* \rb Bilgai,|בִלְגַּ֖י\rb*\f + \fr 10:8 \fqa Bilgai \ft is a variant of \fqa Bilgah\ft ; see \ref Nehemiah 12:5|NEH 12:5\ref*.\f* \rb and Shemaiah.|שְׁמַֽעְיָ֑ה\rb*
\li2 \rb These were|אֵ֖לֶּה\rb* \rb the priests.|הַכֹּהֲנִֽים׃ס\rb*
\p \v 9 \rb The Levites:|וְֽהַלְוִיִּ֑ם\rb*
\b 
\li1 \rb Jeshua|וְיֵשׁ֙וּעַ֙\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Azaniah,|אֲזַנְיָ֔ה\rb*
\li1 \rb Binnui|בִּנּ֕וּי\rb* \rb of the sons|מִבְּנֵ֥י\rb* \rb of Henadad,|חֵנָדָ֖ד\rb* \rb Kadmiel,|קַדְמִיאֵֽל׃\rb*
\li1 \v 10 \rb and their associates:|וַאֲחֵיהֶ֑ם\rb* \rb Shebaniah,|שְׁבַנְיָ֧ה\rb* \rb Hodiah,|הֽוֹדִיָּ֛ה\rb* \rb Kelita,|קְלִיטָ֖א\rb* \rb Pelaiah,|פְּלָאיָ֥ה\rb* \rb Hanan,|חָנָֽן׃\rb*
\li1 \v 11 \rb Mica,|מִיכָ֥א\rb* \rb Rehob,|רְח֖וֹב\rb* \rb Hashabiah,|חֲשַׁבְיָֽה׃\rb*
\li1 \v 12 \rb Zaccur,|זַכּ֥וּר\rb* \rb Sherebiah,|שֵׁרֵֽבְיָ֖ה\rb* \rb Shebaniah,|שְׁבַנְיָֽה׃\rb*
\li1 \v 13 \rb Hodiah,|הוֹדִיָּ֥ה\rb* \rb Bani,|בָנִ֖י\rb* \rb and Beninu.|בְּנִֽינוּ׃ס\rb*
\p \v 14 \rb And the leaders|רָאשֵׁ֖י\rb* \rb of the people:|הָעָ֑ם\rb*
\b 
\li1 \rb Parosh,|פַּרְעֹשׁ֙\rb*\rb |פַּחַ֣ת\rb* \rb Pahath-moab,|מוֹאָ֔ב\rb* \rb Elam,|עֵילָ֥ם\rb* \rb Zattu,|זַתּ֖וּא\rb* \rb Bani,|בָּנִֽי׃\rb*
\li1 \v 15 \rb Bunni,|בֻּנִּ֥י\rb* \rb Azgad,|עַזְגָּ֖ד\rb* \rb Bebai,|בֵּבָֽי׃\rb*
\li1 \v 16 \rb Adonijah,|אֲדֹנִיָּ֥ה\rb* \rb Bigvai,|בִגְוַ֖י\rb* \rb Adin,|עָדִֽין׃\rb*
\li1 \v 17 \rb Ater,|אָטֵ֥ר\rb* \rb Hezekiah,|חִזְקִיָּ֖ה\rb* \rb Azzur,|עַזּֽוּר׃\rb*
\li1 \v 18 \rb Hodiah,|הוֹדִיָּ֥ה\rb* \rb Hashum,|חָשֻׁ֖ם\rb* \rb Bezai,|בֵּצָֽי׃\rb*
\li1 \v 19 \rb Hariph,|חָרִ֥יף\rb* \rb Anathoth,|עֲנָת֖וֹת\rb* \rb Nebai,|נוֹבָי׃\rb*
\li1 \v 20 \rb Magpiash,|מַגְפִּיעָ֥שׁ\rb* \rb Meshullam,|מְשֻׁלָּ֖ם\rb* \rb Hezir,|חֵזִֽיר׃\rb*
\li1 \v 21 \rb Meshezabel,|מְשֵׁיזַבְאֵ֥ל\rb* \rb Zadok,|צָד֖וֹק\rb* \rb Jaddua,|יַדּֽוּעַ׃\rb*
\li1 \v 22 \rb Pelatiah,|פְּלַטְיָ֥ה\rb* \rb Hanan,|חָנָ֖ן\rb* \rb Anaiah,|עֲנָיָֽה׃\rb*
\li1 \v 23 \rb Hoshea,|הוֹשֵׁ֥עַ\rb* \rb Hananiah,|חֲנַנְיָ֖ה\rb* \rb Hasshub,|חַשּֽׁוּב׃\rb*
\li1 \v 24 \rb Hallohesh,|הַלּוֹחֵ֥שׁ\rb* \rb Pilha,|פִּלְחָ֖א\rb* \rb Shobek,|שׁוֹבֵֽק׃\rb*
\li1 \v 25 \rb Rehum,|רְח֥וּם\rb* \rb Hashabnah,|חֲשַׁבְנָ֖ה\rb* \rb Maaseiah,|מַעֲשֵׂיָֽה׃\rb*
\li1 \v 26 \rb Ahijah,|וַאֲחִיָּ֥ה\rb* \rb Hanan,|חָנָ֖ן\rb* \rb Anan,|עָנָֽן׃\rb*
\li1 \v 27 \rb Malluch,|מַלּ֥וּךְ\rb* \rb Harim,|חָרִ֖ם\rb* \rb and Baanah.|בַּעֲנָֽה׃\rb*
\s1 The Vows of the Covenant
\p \v 28 \rb “The rest|וּשְׁאָ֣ר\rb* \rb of the people—|הָעָ֡ם\rb* \rb the priests,|הַכֹּהֲנִ֣ים\rb* \rb Levites,|הַ֠לְוִיִּם\rb* \rb gatekeepers,|הַשּׁוֹעֲרִ֨ים\rb* \rb singers,|הַמְשֹׁרְרִ֜ים\rb* \rb temple servants,|הַנְּתִינִ֗ים\rb*\f + \fr 10:28 \ft Hebrew \fqa Nethinim\f* \rb and all|וְֽכָל־\rb* \rb who had separated themselves|הַנִּבְדָּ֞ל\rb* \rb from the people|מֵעַמֵּ֤י\rb* \rb of the land|הָאֲרָצוֹת֙\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb obey the Law|תּוֹרַ֣ת\rb* \rb of God—|הָאֱלֹהִ֔ים\rb* \rb along with their wives|נְשֵׁיהֶ֖ם\rb* \rb and all|כֹּ֖ל\rb* \rb their sons|בְּנֵיהֶ֣ם\rb* \rb and daughters|וּבְנֹתֵיהֶ֑ם\rb*\rb |יוֹדֵ֥עַ\rb* \rb who are able to understand,|מֵבִֽין׃\rb* \v 29 \rb hereby join|מַחֲזִיקִ֣ים\rb* \rb with|עַל־\rb* \rb their noble|אַדִּירֵיהֶם֒\rb* \rb brothers|אֲחֵיהֶם֮\rb* \rb and commit|וּבָאִ֞ים\rb* \rb themselves with a sworn|וּבִשְׁבוּעָ֗ה\rb* \rb oath|בְּאָלָ֣ה\rb* \rb to follow|לָלֶ֙כֶת֙\rb* \rb the Law|בְּתוֹרַ֣ת\rb* \rb of God|הָאֱלֹהִ֔ים\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb given|נִתְּנָ֔ה\rb* \rb through|בְּיַ֖ד\rb* \rb His|הָֽאֱלֹהִ֑ים\rb* \rb servant|עֶֽבֶד־\rb* \rb Moses|מֹשֶׁ֣ה\rb* \rb and to obey|וְלַעֲשׂ֗וֹת\rb* \rb carefully|וְלִשְׁמ֣וֹר\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the commandments,|מִצְוֺת֙\rb* \rb ordinances,|וּמִשְׁפָּטָ֖יו\rb* \rb and statutes|וְחֻקָּֽיו׃\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb our Lord.|אֲדֹנֵ֔ינוּ\rb*
\p \v 30 \rb |וַאֲשֶׁ֛ר\rb* \rb We will not|לֹא־\rb* \rb give|נִתֵּ֥ן\rb* \rb our daughters in marriage|בְּנֹתֵ֖ינוּ\rb* \rb to the people|לְעַמֵּ֣י\rb* \rb of the land,|הָאָ֑רֶץ\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and we will not|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb take|נִקַּ֖ח\rb* \rb their daughters|בְּנֹ֣תֵיהֶ֔ם\rb* \rb for our sons.|לְבָנֵֽינוּ׃\rb*
\p \v 31 \rb When the people|וְעַמֵּ֣י\rb* \rb of the land|הָאָ֡רֶץ\rb* \rb bring|הַֽמְבִיאִים֩\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb merchandise|הַמַּקָּח֨וֹת\rb* \rb or any|וְכָל־\rb* \rb kind of grain|שֶׁ֜בֶר\rb* \rb to sell|לִמְכּ֔וֹר\rb* \rb on the Sabbath|הַשַּׁבָּת֙\rb* \rb day,|בְּי֤וֹם\rb* \rb we will not|לֹא־\rb* \rb buy|נִקַּ֥ח\rb* \rb from them|מֵהֶ֛ם\rb* \rb on a Sabbath|בַּשַּׁבָּ֖ת\rb* \rb or holy|קֹ֑דֶשׁ\rb* \rb day.|וּבְי֣וֹם\rb* \rb Every seventh|הַשְּׁבִיעִ֖ית\rb* \rb year|הַשָּׁנָ֥ה\rb* \rb we will let the fields lie fallow|וְנִטֹּ֛שׁ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb and will cancel every|כָל־\rb*\rb |יָֽד׃\rb* \rb debt.|וּמַשָּׁ֥א\rb*
\p \v 32 \rb We also place|וְהֶעֱמַ֤דְנוּ\rb* \rb ourselves|עָלֵ֛ינוּ\rb* \rb under|עָלֵ֙ינוּ֙\rb* \rb the obligation|מִצְוֺ֔ת\rb* \rb to contribute|לָתֵ֥ת\rb* \rb a third|שְׁלִשִׁ֥ית\rb* \rb of a shekel|הַשֶּׁ֖קֶל\rb*\f + \fr 10:32 \fqa A third of a shekel \ft is approximately 0.13 ounces or 3.8 grams, probably of silver.\f* \rb yearly|בַּשָּׁנָ֑ה\rb* \rb for the service|לַעֲבֹדַ֖ת\rb* \rb of the house|בֵּ֥ית\rb* \rb of our God:|אֱלֹהֵֽינוּ׃\rb* \v 33 \rb for the showbread,|לְלֶ֣חֶם\rb*\rb |הַֽמַּעֲרֶ֡כֶת\rb* \rb for the regular|הַתָּמִ֣יד\rb* \rb grain offerings|וּמִנְחַ֣ת\rb*\rb |הַ֠תָּמִיד\rb* \rb and burnt offerings,|וּלְעוֹלַ֣ת\rb* \rb for the Sabbath offerings,|הַשַּׁבָּת֨וֹת\rb* \rb for the New Moons|הֶחֳדָשִׁ֜ים\rb* \rb and appointed feasts,|לַמּוֹעֲדִ֗ים\rb* \rb for the holy offerings,|וְלַקֳּדָשִׁים֙\rb* \rb for the sin offerings|וְלַ֣חַטָּא֔וֹת\rb* \rb to make atonement|לְכַפֵּ֖ר\rb* \rb for|עַל־\rb* \rb Israel,|יִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb* \rb and for all|וְכֹ֖ל\rb* \rb the duties|מְלֶ֥אכֶת\rb* \rb of the house|בֵּית־\rb* \rb of our God.|אֱלֹהֵֽינוּ׃ס\rb*
\p \v 34 \rb We have cast|הִפַּ֜לְנוּ\rb* \rb lots|וְהַגּוֹרָל֨וֹת\rb* \rb among the priests,|הַכֹּהֲנִ֣ים\rb* \rb Levites,|הַלְוִיִּם֮\rb* \rb and people|וְהָעָם֒\rb* \rb for|עַל־\rb* \rb the donation|קֻרְבַּ֣ן\rb* \rb of wood|הָעֵצִ֗ים\rb* \rb by our families|לְבֵית־\rb*\rb |אֲבֹתֵ֛ינוּ\rb* \rb at the appointed|מְזֻמָּנִ֖ים\rb* \rb times|לְעִתִּ֥ים\rb* \rb each year.|שָׁנָ֣ה\rb*\rb |בְשָׁנָ֑ה\rb* \rb They are to bring it|לְ֠הָבִיא\rb* \rb to the house|לְבֵ֨ית\rb* \rb of our God|אֱלֹהֵ֧ינוּ\rb* \rb to burn|לְבַעֵ֗ר\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb the altar|מִזְבַּח֙\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb our God,|אֱלֹהֵ֔ינוּ\rb* \rb as it is written|כַּכָּת֖וּב\rb* \rb in the Law.|בַּתּוֹרָֽה׃\rb*
\p \v 35 \rb We will also bring|וּלְהָבִ֞יא\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the firstfruits|בִּכּוּרֵ֣י\rb* \rb of our land|אַדְמָתֵ֗נוּ\rb*\rb |וּבִכּוּרֵ֛י\rb* \rb and of every|כָּל־\rb* \rb fruit|פְּרִ֥י\rb*\rb |כָל־\rb* \rb tree|עֵ֖ץ\rb* \rb to the house|לְבֵ֖ית\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָֽה׃\rb* \rb year|שָׁנָ֣ה\rb* \rb by year.|בְשָׁנָ֑ה\rb* \v 36 \rb And|וְאֶת־\rb* \rb we will bring|לְהָבִיא֙\rb* \rb the firstborn|בְּכֹר֤וֹת\rb* \rb of our sons|בָּנֵ֙ינוּ֙\rb* \rb and our livestock,|וּבְהֶמְתֵּ֔ינוּ\rb* \rb as it is written|כַּכָּת֖וּב\rb* \rb in the Law,|בַּתּוֹרָ֑ה\rb* \rb and|וְאֶת־\rb* \rb will bring the firstborn|בְּכוֹרֵ֨י\rb* \rb of our herds|בְקָרֵ֜ינוּ\rb* \rb and flocks|וְצֹאנֵ֗ינוּ\rb* \rb to the house|לְבֵ֣ית\rb* \rb of our God,|אֱלֹהֵ֔ינוּ\rb* \rb to the priests|לַכֹּ֣הֲנִ֔ים\rb* \rb who minister|הַמְשָׁרְתִ֖ים\rb* \rb in the house|בְּבֵ֥ית\rb* \rb of our God.|אֱלֹהֵֽינוּ׃\rb*
