\s1 Jerusalem’s New Settlers
\p \v 1 \rb Now the leaders|שָׂרֵֽי־\rb* \rb of the people|הָעָ֖ם\rb* \rb settled|וַיֵּשְׁב֥וּ\rb* \rb in Jerusalem,|בִּירוּשָׁלִָ֑ם\rb* \rb and the rest|וּשְׁאָ֣ר\rb* \rb of the people|הָ֠עָם\rb* \rb cast|הִפִּ֨ילוּ\rb* \rb lots|גוֹרָל֜וֹת\rb* \rb to bring|לְהָבִ֣יא׀\rb* \rb one|אֶחָ֣ד\rb* \rb out|מִן־\rb* \rb of ten|הָעֲשָׂרָ֗ה\rb* \rb to live|לָשֶׁ֙בֶת֙\rb* \rb in the holy|הַקֹּ֔דֶשׁ\rb* \rb city|עִ֣יר\rb* \rb of Jerusalem,|בִּֽירוּשָׁלִַ֙ם֙\rb* \rb while|וְתֵ֥שַׁע\rb* \rb the remaining nine|הַיָּד֖וֹת\rb*\f + \fr 11:1 \ft Hebrew \fqa nine hands\f* \rb were to dwell in their own towns.|בֶּעָרִֽים׃\rb* \v 2 \rb And the people|הָעָ֑ם\rb* \rb blessed|וַֽיְבָרֲכ֖וּ\rb* \rb all|לְכֹל֙\rb* \rb the men|הָֽאֲנָשִׁ֔ים\rb* \rb who volunteered|הַמִּֽתְנַדְּבִ֔ים\rb* \rb to live|לָשֶׁ֖בֶת\rb* \rb in Jerusalem.|בִּירוּשָׁלִָֽם׃פ\rb*
\p \v 3 \rb These|וְאֵ֙לֶּה֙\rb* \rb are the heads|רָאשֵׁ֣י\rb* \rb of the provinces|הַמְּדִינָ֔ה\rb* \rb who|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb settled|יָשְׁב֖וּ\rb* \rb in Jerusalem.|בִּירוּשָׁלִָ֑ם\rb* \rb (In the villages|וּבְעָרֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Judah, however,|יְהוּדָ֗ה\rb* \rb each|אִ֤ישׁ\rb* \rb lived|יָֽשְׁב֞וּ\rb* \rb on his own property|בַּאֲחֻזָּתוֹ֙\rb* \rb in their towns—|בְּעָ֣רֵיהֶ֔ם\rb* \rb the Israelites,|יִשְׂרָאֵ֤ל\rb* \rb priests,|הַכֹּהֲנִים֙\rb* \rb Levites,|וְהַלְוִיִּ֣ם\rb* \rb temple servants,|וְהַנְּתִינִ֔ים\rb*\f + \fr 11:3 \ft Hebrew \fqa Nethinim\ft ; also in verse 21\f* \rb and descendants|וּבְנֵ֖י\rb* \rb of Solomon’s|שְׁלֹמֹֽה׃\rb* \rb servants—|עַבְדֵ֥י\rb* \v 4 \rb while some of the descendants|מִבְּנֵ֥י\rb* \rb of Judah|יְהוּדָ֖ה\rb* \rb and Benjamin|בִנְיָמִ֑ן\rb* \rb settled|יָֽשְׁב֔וּ\rb* \rb in Jerusalem.)|וּבִֽירוּשָׁלִַ֙ם֙\rb*
