\c 13
\s1 Foreigners Excluded
\p \v 1 \rb At that|הַה֗וּא\rb* \rb time|בַּיּ֣וֹם\rb* \rb the Book|בְּסֵ֥פֶר\rb* \rb of Moses|מֹשֶׁ֖ה\rb* \rb was read aloud|נִקְרָ֛א\rb* \rb in the hearing|בְּאָזְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb of the people,|הָעָ֑ם\rb* \rb and in it|בּ֔וֹ\rb* \rb they found|וְנִמְצָא֙\rb* \rb the passage stating|כָּת֣וּב\rb* \rb that|אֲ֠שֶׁר\rb* \rb no|לֹא־\rb* \rb Ammonite|עַמֹּנִ֧י\rb* \rb or Moabite|וּמֹאָבִ֛י\rb* \rb should ever|עַד־\rb*\rb |עוֹלָֽם׃\rb* \rb enter|יָב֨וֹא\rb* \rb the assembly|בִּקְהַ֥ל\rb* \rb of God,|הָאֱלֹהִ֖ים\rb*\f + \fr 13:1 \ft See \ref Deuteronomy 23:3–6|DEU 23:3-6\ref*.\f* \v 2 \rb because|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb they had not|לֹ֧א\rb* \rb met|קִדְּמ֛וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the Israelites|בְּנֵ֥י\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל\rb* \rb with food|בַּלֶּ֣חֶם\rb* \rb and water,|וּבַמָּ֑יִם\rb* \rb but had hired|וַיִּשְׂכֹּ֨ר\rb* \rb Balaam|בִּלְעָם֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb to call down a curse|לְקַֽלְל֔וֹ\rb* \rb against them|עָלָ֤יו\rb* \rb (although our God|אֱלֹהֵ֛ינוּ\rb* \rb had turned|וַיַּהֲפֹ֧ךְ\rb* \rb the curse|הַקְּלָלָ֖ה\rb* \rb into a blessing).|לִבְרָכָֽה׃\rb*
