\s1 The Temple Cleansed
\p \v 4 \rb Now before|וְלִפְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb this,|מִזֶּ֔ה\rb* \rb Eliashib|אֶלְיָשִׁיב֙\rb* \rb the priest,|הַכֹּהֵ֔ן\rb* \rb a relative|קָר֖וֹב\rb* \rb of Tobiah,|לְטוֹבִיָּֽה׃\rb* \rb had been put in charge of|נָת֖וּן\rb* \rb the storerooms|בְּלִשְׁכַּ֣ת\rb* \rb of the house|בֵּית־\rb* \rb of our God|אֱלֹהֵ֑ינוּ\rb* \v 5 \rb and had prepared|וַיַּ֨עַשׂ\rb* \rb for Tobiah|ל֜וֹ\rb* \rb a large|גְדוֹלָ֗ה\rb* \rb room|לִשְׁכָּ֣ה\rb* \rb where|וְשָׁ֣ם\rb*\rb |הָי֪וּ\rb* \rb they had previously|לְפָנִ֟ים\rb* \rb stored|נֹ֠תְנִים\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the grain offerings,|הַמִּנְחָ֨ה\rb* \rb the frankincense,|הַלְּבוֹנָ֜ה\rb* \rb the temple articles,|וְהַכֵּלִ֗ים\rb* \rb and the tithes|וּמַעְשַׂ֤ר\rb* \rb of grain,|הַדָּגָן֙\rb* \rb new wine,|הַתִּיר֣וֹשׁ\rb* \rb and oil|וְהַיִּצְהָ֔ר\rb* \rb prescribed|מִצְוַת֙\rb* \rb for the Levites,|הַלְוִיִּ֔ם\rb* \rb singers,|וְהַמְשֹׁרְרִ֖ים\rb* \rb and gatekeepers,|וְהַשֹּׁעֲרִ֑ים\rb* \rb along with the contributions|וּתְרוּמַ֖ת\rb* \rb for the priests.|הַכֹּהֲנִֽים׃\rb*
\p \v 6 \rb While all|וּבְכָל־\rb* \rb this|זֶ֕ה\rb* \rb was happening,|הָיִ֖יתִי\rb* \rb I was not|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb in Jerusalem,|בִּֽירוּשָׁלִָ֑ם\rb* \rb because|כִּ֡י\rb* \rb I had returned|בָּ֣אתִי\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Artaxerxes|לְאַרְתַּחְשַׁ֤סְתְּא\rb* \rb king|מֶֽלֶךְ־\rb* \rb of Babylon|בָּבֶל֙\rb*\f + \fr 13:6 \ft Artaxerxes king of Persia is identified here as the king of Babylon because Persia had conquered the Babylonian Empire.\f* \rb in the thirty-second|שְׁלֹשִׁ֨ים\rb*\rb |וּשְׁתַּ֜יִם\rb* \rb year|בִּשְׁנַת֩\rb* \rb of his reign.|הַמֶּ֔לֶךְ\rb* \rb Some time later|וּלְקֵ֥ץ\rb*\rb |יָמִ֖ים\rb* \rb I obtained leave|נִשְׁאַ֥לְתִּי\rb* \rb from|מִן־\rb* \rb the king|הַמֶּֽלֶךְ׃\rb* \v 7 \rb to return|וָאָב֖וֹא\rb* \rb to Jerusalem.|לִֽירוּשָׁלִָ֑ם\rb* \rb Then I discovered|וָאָבִ֣ינָה\rb* \rb the evil|בָרָעָ֗ה\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb Eliashib|אֶלְיָשִׁיב֙\rb* \rb had done|עָשָׂ֤ה\rb* \rb on behalf of Tobiah|לְט֣וֹבִיָּ֔ה\rb* \rb by providing|לַעֲשׂ֥וֹת\rb* \rb him|לוֹ֙\rb* \rb a room|נִשְׁכָּ֔ה\rb* \rb in the courts|בְּחַצְרֵ֖י\rb* \rb of the house|בֵּ֥ית\rb* \rb of God.|הָאֱלֹהִֽים׃\rb*
\p \v 8 \rb And I was greatly|מְאֹ֑ד\rb* \rb displeased|וַיֵּ֥רַֽע\rb* \rb and threw|וָֽאַשְׁלִ֜יכָה\rb*\rb |אֶֽת־\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb of Tobiah’s|טוֹבִיָּ֛ה\rb* \rb household|בֵית־\rb* \rb goods|כְּלֵ֧י\rb* \rb out|הַח֖וּץ\rb* \rb of|מִן־\rb* \rb the room.|הַלִּשְׁכָּֽה׃\rb* \v 9 \rb Then I ordered|וָאֹ֣מְרָ֔ה\rb* \rb that the rooms|הַלְּשָׁכ֑וֹת\rb* \rb be purified,|וַֽיְטַהֲר֖וּ\rb* \rb and I had the articles|כְּלֵי֙\rb* \rb of the house|בֵּ֣ית\rb* \rb of God|הָאֱלֹהִ֔ים\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb restored|וָאָשִׁ֣יבָה\rb* \rb to them,|שָּׁ֗ם\rb* \rb along with the grain offerings|הַמִּנְחָ֖ה\rb* \rb and frankincense.|וְהַלְּבוֹנָֽה׃פ\rb*
\s1 Tithes Restored
