\p \v 10 \rb I also learned|וָאֵ֣דְעָ֔ה\rb* \rb that|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb because the portions|מְנָי֥וֹת\rb* \rb for the Levites|הַלְוִיִּ֖ם\rb* \rb had not|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb been given to them,|נִתָּ֑נָה\rb* \rb all|אִישׁ־\rb* \rb the Levites|הַלְוִיִּ֥ם\rb* \rb and singers|וְהַמְשֹׁרְרִ֖ים\rb* \rb responsible for performing|עֹשֵׂ֥י\rb* \rb the service|הַמְּלָאכָֽה׃\rb* \rb had gone back|וַיִּבְרְח֧וּ\rb* \rb to their own fields.|לְשָׂדֵ֛הוּ\rb* \v 11 \rb So I rebuked|וָאָרִ֙יבָה֙\rb* \rb the officials|הַסְּגָנִ֔ים\rb* \rb and asked,|וָאֹ֣מְרָ֔ה\rb* \rb “Why|מַדּ֖וּעַ\rb* \rb has the house|בֵּית־\rb* \rb of God|הָאֱלֹהִ֑ים\rb* \rb been neglected?”|נֶעֱזַ֣ב\rb*
\p \rb Then I gathered the Levites and singers together|וָֽאֶ֨קְבְּצֵ֔ם\rb* \rb and stationed them|וָֽאַעֲמִדֵ֖ם\rb* \rb at|עַל־\rb* \rb their posts,|עָמְדָֽם׃\rb* \v 12 \rb and all|וְכָל־\rb* \rb Judah|יְהוּדָ֗ה\rb* \rb brought|הֵבִ֜יאוּ\rb* \rb a tenth|מַעְשַׂ֧ר\rb* \rb of the grain,|הַדָּגָ֛ן\rb* \rb new wine,|וְהַתִּיר֥וֹשׁ\rb* \rb and oil|וְהַיִּצְהָ֖ר\rb* \rb into the storerooms.|לָאוֹצָרֽוֹת׃\rb* \v 13 \rb I appointed as treasurers|וָאוֹצְרָ֣ה\rb* \rb over|עַל־\rb* \rb the storerooms|א֠וֹצָרוֹת\rb* \rb Shelemiah|שֶׁלֶמְיָ֨ה\rb* \rb the priest,|הַכֹּהֵ֜ן\rb* \rb Zadok|וְצָד֣וֹק\rb* \rb the scribe,|הַסּוֹפֵ֗ר\rb* \rb and Pedaiah|וּפְדָיָה֙\rb* \rb of|מִן־\rb* \rb the Levites,|הַלְוִיִּ֔ם\rb* \rb with Hanan|חָנָ֥ן\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Zaccur,|זַכּ֖וּר\rb* \rb the son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Mattaniah,|מַתַּנְיָ֑ה\rb* \rb to assist|וְעַל־\rb* \rb them,|יָדָ֔ם\rb* \rb because|כִּ֤י\rb* \rb they were considered|נֶחְשָׁ֔בוּ\rb* \rb trustworthy.|נֶאֱמָנִים֙\rb* \rb They were responsible for|וַעֲלֵיהֶ֖ם\rb* \rb distributing the supplies|לַחֲלֹ֥ק\rb* \rb to their fellow Levites.|לַאֲחֵיהֶֽם׃פ\rb*
\p \v 14 \rb Remember|זָכְרָה־\rb* \rb me|לִּ֥י\rb* \rb for|עַל־\rb* \rb this,|זֹ֑את\rb* \rb O my God,|אֱלֹהַ֖י\rb* \rb and do not|וְאַל־\rb* \rb blot out|תֶּ֣מַח\rb* \rb my deeds of loving devotion|חֲסָדַ֗י\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb*\rb |עָשִׂ֛יתִי\rb* \rb for the house|בְּבֵ֥ית\rb* \rb of my God|אֱלֹהַ֖י\rb* \rb and for its services.|וּבְמִשְׁמָרָֽיו׃\rb*
\s1 The Sabbath Restored
\r \ref Jeremiah 17:19–27|JER 17:19-27\ref*)
\p \v 15 \rb In those|הָהֵ֡מָּה\rb* \rb days|בַּיָּמִ֣ים\rb* \rb I saw|רָאִ֣יתִי\rb* \rb people in Judah|בִֽיהוּדָ֣ה׀\rb* \rb treading|דֹּֽרְכִֽים־\rb* \rb winepresses|גִּתּ֣וֹת׀\rb* \rb on the Sabbath|בַּשַּׁבָּ֡ת\rb* \rb and bringing in|וּמְבִיאִ֣ים\rb* \rb grain|הָעֲרֵמ֣וֹת\rb* \rb and loading it|וְֽעֹמְסִ֪ים\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb donkeys,|הַחֲמֹרִ֟ים\rb* \rb along with|וְאַף־\rb* \rb wine,|יַ֜יִן\rb* \rb grapes,|עֲנָבִ֤ים\rb* \rb and figs.|וּתְאֵנִים֙\rb* \rb All kinds|וְכָל־\rb* \rb of goods|מַשָּׂ֔א\rb* \rb were being brought|וּמְבִיאִ֥ים\rb* \rb into Jerusalem|יְרוּשָׁלִַ֖ם\rb* \rb on the Sabbath|הַשַּׁבָּ֑ת\rb* \rb day.|בְּי֣וֹם\rb* \rb So I warned them|וָאָעִ֕יד\rb* \rb against selling|מִכְרָ֥ם\rb* \rb food|צָֽיִד׃\rb* \rb on that day.|בְּי֖וֹם\rb* \v 16 \rb Additionally, men of Tyre|וְהַצֹּרִים֙\rb* \rb who lived|יָ֣שְׁבוּ\rb* \rb there|בָ֔הּ\rb* \rb were importing|מְבִיאִ֥ים\rb* \rb fish|דָּ֖אג\rb* \rb and all kinds|וְכָל־\rb* \rb of merchandise|מֶ֑כֶר\rb* \rb and selling them|וּמֹכְרִ֧ים\rb* \rb on the Sabbath|בַּשַּׁבָּ֛ת\rb* \rb to the people|לִבְנֵ֥י\rb* \rb of Judah|יְהוּדָ֖ה\rb* \rb in Jerusalem.|וּבִירוּשָׁלִָֽם׃\rb*
\p \v 17 \rb Then I rebuked|וָאָרִ֕יבָה\rb*\rb |אֵ֖ת\rb* \rb the nobles|חֹרֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Judah|יְהוּדָ֑ה\rb* \rb and asked,|וָאֹמְרָ֣ה\rb* \rb “What|מָֽה־\rb*\rb |הַדָּבָ֨ר\rb* \rb is this|הַזֶּה֙\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb evil|הָרָ֤ע\rb* \rb you|אַתֶּ֣ם\rb* \rb are doing—|עֹשִׂ֔ים\rb* \rb profaning|וּֽמְחַלְּלִ֖ים\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the Sabbath|הַשַּׁבָּֽת׃\rb* \rb day?|י֥וֹם\rb* \v 18 \rb Did not|הֲל֨וֹא\rb* \rb your forefathers|אֲבֹ֣תֵיכֶ֔ם\rb* \rb do|עָשׂוּ֙\rb* \rb the same things,|כֹ֤ה\rb* \rb so that our God|אֱלֹהֵ֜ינוּ\rb* \rb brought|וַיָּבֵ֨א\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb this|הַזֹּ֔את\rb* \rb disaster|הָרָעָ֣ה\rb* \rb on us|עָלֵ֗ינוּ\rb*\rb |אֵ֚ת\rb* \rb and on|וְעַ֖ל\rb* \rb this|הַזֹּ֑את\rb* \rb city?|הָעִ֣יר\rb* \rb And now|וְאַתֶּ֞ם\rb* \rb you are rekindling|מוֹסִיפִ֤ים\rb* \rb His wrath|חָרוֹן֙\rb* \rb against|עַל־\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb* \rb by profaning|לְחַלֵּ֖ל\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the Sabbath!”|הַשַּׁבָּֽת׃פ\rb*
\p \v 19 \rb |וַיְהִ֡י\rb* \rb When|כַּאֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb the evening shadows|צָֽלֲלוּ֩\rb* \rb began to fall on the gates|שַׁעֲרֵ֨י\rb* \rb of Jerusalem,|יְרוּשָׁלִַ֜ם\rb* \rb just before|לִפְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb the Sabbath,|הַשַּׁבָּ֗ת\rb* \rb I ordered|וָאֹֽמְרָה֙\rb* \rb that the gates|הַדְּלָת֔וֹת\rb*\rb |וָאֹ֣מְרָ֔ה\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר֙\rb* \rb be shut|וַיִּסָּגְר֣וּ\rb* \rb and not|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb opened|יִפְתָּח֔וּם\rb* \rb until|עַ֖ד\rb* \rb after|אַחַ֣ר\rb* \rb the Sabbath.|הַשַּׁבָּ֑ת\rb* \rb I posted|הֶֽעֱמַ֙דְתִּי֙\rb* \rb some of my servants|וּמִנְּעָרַ֗י\rb* \rb at|עַל־\rb* \rb the gates|הַשְּׁעָרִ֔ים\rb* \rb so that no|לֹא־\rb* \rb load|מַשָּׂ֖א\rb* \rb could enter|יָב֥וֹא\rb* \rb on the Sabbath|הַשַּׁבָּֽת׃\rb* \rb day.|בְּי֥וֹם\rb*
\p \v 20 \rb Once|פַּ֥עַם\rb* \rb or twice,|וּשְׁתָּֽיִם׃\rb* \rb the merchants|הָרֹכְלִ֜ים\rb* \rb and those who sell|וּמֹכְרֵ֧י\rb* \rb all kinds|כָל־\rb* \rb of goods|מִמְכָּ֛ר\rb* \rb camped|וַיָּלִ֨ינוּ\rb* \rb outside|מִח֥וּץ\rb* \rb Jerusalem,|לִירוּשָׁלִָ֖ם\rb* \v 21 \rb but I warned|וָאָעִ֣ידָה\rb* \rb them,|בָהֶ֗ם\rb*\rb |וָאֹמְרָ֤ה\rb*\rb |אֲלֵיהֶם֙\rb* \rb “Why|מַדּ֜וּעַ\rb* \rb are you|אַתֶּ֤ם\rb* \rb camping|לֵנִים֙\rb* \rb in front of|נֶ֣גֶד\rb* \rb the wall?|הַחוֹמָ֔ה\rb* \rb If|אִם־\rb* \rb you do it again,|תִּשְׁנ֕וּ\rb* \rb I will lay|אֶשְׁלַ֣ח\rb* \rb hands|יָ֖ד\rb* \rb on you.”|בָּכֶ֑ם\rb* \rb From|מִן־\rb* \rb that|הַהִ֔יא\rb* \rb time on,|הָעֵ֣ת\rb* \rb they did not|לֹא־\rb* \rb return|בָ֖אוּ\rb* \rb on the Sabbath.|בַּשַּׁבָּֽת׃ס\rb* \v 22 \rb Then I instructed|וָאֹמְרָ֣ה\rb* \rb the Levites|לַלְוִיִּ֗ם\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb*\rb |יִֽהְי֤וּ\rb* \rb to purify themselves|מִֽטַּהֲרִים֙\rb*\rb |וּבָאִים֙\rb* \rb and guard|שֹׁמְרִ֣ים\rb* \rb the gates|הַשְּׁעָרִ֔ים\rb* \rb in order to keep the Sabbath|הַשַּׁבָּ֑ת\rb* \rb day|י֣וֹם\rb* \rb holy.|לְקַדֵּ֖שׁ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb*
\p \rb Remember|זָכְרָה־\rb* \rb me|לִּ֣י\rb* \rb for this|זֹאת֙\rb* \rb as well,|גַּם־\rb* \rb O my God,|אֱלֹהַ֔י\rb* \rb and show me|עָלַ֖י\rb* \rb mercy|וְח֥וּסָה\rb* \rb according to Your abundant|כְּרֹ֥ב\rb* \rb loving devotion.|חַסְדֶּֽךָ׃פ\rb*
\s1 Intermarriage Forbidden
\r \ref Ezra 9:1–4|EZR 9:1-4\ref*)
\p \v 23 \rb In those|הָהֵ֗ם\rb* \rb days|בַּיָּמִ֣ים\rb* \rb I also|גַּ֣ם׀\rb* \rb saw|רָאִ֤יתִי\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Jews|הַיְּהוּדִים֙\rb* \rb who had married|הֹשִׁ֗יבוּ\rb* \rb women|נָשִׁים֙\rb* \rb from Ashdod,|אַשְׁדּוֹדִיּוֹת\rb* \rb Ammon,|עַמּוֹנִיּוֹת\rb* \rb and Moab.|מוֹאֲבִיּֽוֹת׃\rb* \v 24 \rb Half|חֲצִי֙\rb* \rb of their children|וּבְנֵיהֶ֗ם\rb* \rb spoke|מְדַבֵּ֣ר\rb* \rb the language of Ashdod|אַשְׁדּוֹדִ֔ית\rb* \rb or of|וְכִלְשׁ֖וֹן\rb* \rb the other peoples,|עַ֥ם\rb*\rb |וָעָֽם׃\rb* \rb but could|מַכִּירִ֖ים\rb* \rb not|וְאֵינָ֥ם\rb* \rb speak|לְדַבֵּ֣ר\rb* \rb the language of Judah.|יְהוּדִ֑ית\rb* \v 25 \rb I rebuked them|וָאָרִ֤יב\rb*\rb |עִמָּם֙\rb* \rb and called down curses on them.|וָאֲקַֽלְלֵ֔ם\rb* \rb I beat|וָאַכֶּ֥ה\rb* \rb some of|מֵהֶ֛ם\rb* \rb these men|אֲנָשִׁ֖ים\rb* \rb and pulled out their hair.|וָֽאֶמְרְטֵ֑ם\rb*
\p \rb Then I made them take an oath|וָאַשְׁבִּיעֵ֣ם\rb* \rb before God and said,|בֵּֽאלֹהִ֗ים\rb* \rb “You must not|אִם־\rb* \rb give your daughters|בְנֹֽתֵיכֶם֙\rb* \rb in marriage|תִּתְּנ֤וּ\rb* \rb to their sons|לִבְנֵיהֶ֔ם\rb*\rb |וְאִם־\rb* \rb or take|תִּשְׂאוּ֙\rb* \rb their daughters|מִבְּנֹ֣תֵיהֶ֔ם\rb* \rb as wives for your sons|לִבְנֵיכֶ֖ם\rb* \rb or for yourselves!|וְלָכֶֽם׃\rb* \v 26 \rb Did not|הֲל֣וֹא\rb* \rb King|מֶ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb Solomon|שְׁלֹמֹ֣ה\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֡ל\rb* \rb sin|חָטָֽא־\rb* \rb in|עַל־\rb* \rb matters like this?|אֵ֣לֶּה\rb* \rb There was|הָיָ֨ה\rb* \rb not|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb a king|מֶ֜לֶךְ\rb* \rb like him|כָּמֹ֗הוּ\rb* \rb among many|הָרַבִּים֩\rb* \rb nations,|וּבַגּוֹיִ֣ם\rb* \rb and he was|הָיָ֔ה\rb* \rb loved|וְאָה֤וּב\rb* \rb by his God,|לֵֽאלֹהָיו֙\rb* \rb who|אֱלֹהִ֔ים\rb* \rb made him|וַיִּתְּנֵ֣הוּ\rb* \rb king|מֶ֖לֶךְ\rb* \rb over|עַל־\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb Israel—|יִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb* \rb yet|גַּם־\rb* \rb foreign|הַנָּכְרִיּֽוֹת׃\rb* \rb women|הַנָּשִׁ֖ים\rb*\rb |אוֹת֣וֹ\rb* \rb drew him into sin.|הֶחֱטִ֔יאוּ\rb* \v 27 \rb |וְלָכֶ֣ם\rb* \rb Must we now hear|הֲנִשְׁמַ֗ע\rb* \rb that you too are doing|לַעֲשֹׂת֙\rb*\rb |אֵ֣ת\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb this|הַזֹּ֔את\rb* \rb terrible|הַגְּדוֹלָה֙\rb* \rb evil|הָרָעָ֤ה\rb* \rb and acting unfaithfully|לִמְעֹ֖ל\rb* \rb against our God|בֵּֽאלֹהֵ֑ינוּ\rb* \rb by marrying|לְהֹשִׁ֖יב\rb* \rb foreign|נָכְרִיּֽוֹת׃\rb* \rb women?”|נָשִׁ֥ים\rb*
\p \v 28 \rb Even one of the sons|וּמִבְּנֵ֨י\rb* \rb of Jehoiada|יוֹיָדָ֤ע\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Eliashib|אֶלְיָשִׁיב֙\rb* \rb the high|הַגָּד֔וֹל\rb* \rb priest|הַכֹּהֵ֣ן\rb* \rb had become a son-in-law|חָתָ֖ן\rb* \rb to Sanballat|לְסַנְבַלַּ֣ט\rb* \rb the Horonite.|הַחֹרֹנִ֑י\rb* \rb Therefore I drove him away|וָאַבְרִיחֵ֖הוּ\rb* \rb from me.|מֵעָלָֽי׃\rb*
\p \v 29 \rb Remember|זָכְרָ֥ה\rb* \rb them,|לָהֶ֖ם\rb* \rb O my God,|אֱלֹהָ֑י\rb* \rb because|עַ֚ל\rb* \rb they have defiled|גָּאֳלֵ֣י\rb* \rb the priesthood|הַכְּהֻנָּ֔ה\rb* \rb and the covenant|וּבְרִ֥ית\rb* \rb of the priesthood|הַכְּהֻנָּ֖ה\rb* \rb and of the Levites.|וְהַלְוִיִּֽם׃\rb*
\p \v 30 \rb Thus I purified the priests and Levites|וְטִֽהַרְתִּ֖ים\rb* \rb from everything|מִכָּל־\rb* \rb foreign,|נֵכָ֑ר\rb* \rb and I assigned|וָאַעֲמִ֧ידָה\rb* \rb specific|בִּמְלַאכְתּֽוֹ׃\rb* \rb duties|מִשְׁמָר֛וֹת\rb* \rb to each|אִ֥ישׁ\rb* \rb of the priests|לַכֹּהֲנִ֥ים\rb* \rb and Levites.|וְלַלְוִיִּ֖ם\rb* \v 31 \rb I also arranged for contributions|וּלְקֻרְבַּ֧ן\rb* \rb of wood|הָעֵצִ֛ים\rb* \rb at the appointed|מְזֻמָּנ֖וֹת\rb* \rb times,|בְּעִתִּ֥ים\rb* \rb and for the firstfruits.|וְלַבִּכּוּרִ֑ים\rb*
\p \rb Remember|זָכְרָה־\rb* \rb me,|לִּ֥י\rb* \rb O my God,|אֱלֹהַ֖י\rb* \rb with favor.|לְטוֹבָֽה׃\rb*
